而且它是外观最帅、速度最快、颜色最红的。
AND it's the best-looking and it's
the fastest and it's the reddest.

142
00:08:46,287 --> 00:08:51,275
我知道哈蒙德和詹姆斯觉得我的928保时捷有点闷
I know Hammond and May
think my 928 Porsche is a bit dull

143
00:08:51,275 --> 00:08:54,359
但有个非常好的理由，它对我一点也不闷。
but for one very good reason,
it isn't dull to me.

144
00:08:56,323 --> 00:08:59,339
你们看，1994年，我住在伦敦，
You see, back in 1994, I was
living in London,

145
00:08:59,339 --> 00:09:02,275
那天傍晚，我妈打来电话说
I got a call one evening from my mum

146
00:09:02,275 --> 00:09:06,279
我爸在谢菲尔德的医院危在旦夕，
to say that my dad was desperately
ill in a hospital in Sheffield

147
00:09:06,279 --> 00:09:09,291
我必须立刻赶过去。
and I needed to get
there as quickly as possible.

148
00:09:09,291 --> 00:09:11,363
我正从烤箱里端出鸡来，心里想，
And I'd just taken a chicken
out of the oven and I thought,

149
00:09:11,363 --> 00:09:14,359
“好吧，我把这鸡留给我妈，她还没吃呢”，
"Well, I'll take that for my mum,
cos she won't have eaten",

150
00:09:14,359 --> 00:09:17,331
冲出门外，恰好那周我还有一辆928在试车。
ran outside and I had a 928 on test
that week.

151
00:09:18,347 --> 00:09:22,343
我赶到谢菲尔德时，鸡肉仍热乎乎的
And when I arrived in Sheffield,
the chicken was still warm

152
00:09:22,343 --> 00:09:25,331
我爸还活着。
and my dad was still alive.

153
00:09:25,331 --> 00:09:28,315
事实上他半小时后去世了。
In fact he died half an hour later.

154
00:09:30,359 --> 00:09:35,287
说实话，要是我没开那辆车，
And the truth is, if I hadn't
been driving a car which

155
00:09:35,287 --> 00:09:39,307
那车能悠哉哉地跑到170英里每小时，
could sit quite happily at 170 miles
an hour,

156
00:09:39,307 --> 00:09:42,351
我就没机会和我爸道别。
I wouldn't have had the opportunity
to say goodbye to my dad.

157
00:09:45,303 --> 00:09:49,335
所以对我来说，928……还行。
So as far as I'm concerned
the 928...is all right.

158
00:10:00,295 --> 00:10:03,287
很快我们来到一个相当德式的城镇。
Soon we arrived at a rather
Germanic-looking town.

159
00:10:06,319 --> 00:10:09,327
我们现在所在的城镇叫巴里洛切
This town that we're in now
is called Bariloche

160
00:10:09,327 --> 00:10:14,363
真的没有什么好说的——
and there really is no nice
way of putting this -

161
00:10:14,363 --> 00:10:18,287
它成了纳粹战犯的避风港。
it became a haven for Nazi
war criminals.

162
00:10:20,303 --> 00:10:25,283
从1946年——关键的一年——到1952年，
Between 1946 - a critical date -
and 1952,

163
00:10:25,283 --> 00:10:29,327
有12,000名德国人搬到这片偏僻的地方定居。
12,000 Germans came to live
in this neck of the woods.

164
00:10:29,327 --> 00:10:31,331
创立纳粹青年团的那家伙，
The man who founded
the Hitler Youth,

165
00:10:31,331 --> 00:10:33,327
他在镇上开了滑雪俱乐部。
he started the ski club in the town.

166
00:10:33,327 --> 00:10:37,339
阿道夫·艾希曼住在这里。约瑟夫·门格勒在这里考驾照。
Adolf Eichmann lived here. Josef
Mengele took his driving test here.

167
00:10:37,339 --> 00:10:39,351
显然没过。
Failed, apparently.

168
00:10:43,307 --> 00:10:44,363
是的，话题有点沉重
Yes, it's a sombre topic

169
00:10:44,363 --> 00:10:48,355
但幸好哈蒙德用他的《拉库卡拉查》喇叭把气氛活跃了起来。
but fortunately Hammond's enlivened
it with his La Cucaracha horn.

170
00:10:50,359 --> 00:10:54,319
一离开柏林郊区，路面就开阔了
Once out of Berlineloche,
the roads opened up

171
00:10:54,319 --> 00:10:59,271
哈蒙德就能全速体验他肌肉车的乐趣。
and Hammond could discover the joys
of his muscle car at full chat.

172
00:11:00,287 --> 00:11:04,271
现在速度真猛，说实话，有点吓人，
Big speed now and I'll be honest,
it is quite alarming,

173
00:11:04,271 --> 00:11:06,271
这方向盘感觉……
this steering is...

174
00:11:06,271 --> 00:11:10,271
玩起来太松，而且……感觉有点模糊——是啊。
There's a lot of play and er,
it's kind of vague - yeah.

175
00:11:15,275 --> 00:11:19,283
与此同时，詹姆斯和我已经陷入了一场小小的狗斗。
Meanwhile, James and I have become
entangled in a bit of a dogfight.

176
00:11:20,315 --> 00:11:21,343
目标锁定。
Target locked.

177
00:11:28,347 --> 00:11:30,311
我抓到了他。
I've got him.

178
00:11:30,311 --> 00:11:32,303
不！哈哈！
No! Ha-ha!

179
00:11:33,339 --> 00:11:36,295
哔——！我逮到他在打盹儿了。
Sod it!
I've caught him napping.

180
00:11:36,295 --> 00:11:39,311
你种下风暴，就会收获狂风。
You have sown the wind
and you shall reap the whirlwind.

181
00:11:39,311 --> 00:11:43,279
来啦，来啦，来啦。
Here we go, here we go, here we go.

182
00:11:43,279 --> 00:11:45,351
不，不，不，不，不，不！
No, no, no, no, no, no!

183
00:11:45,351 --> 00:11:47,367
好啊，接招！
Yes. Take that.

184
00:11:49,363 --> 00:11:51,299
呃！
Urgh!

185
00:11:54,279 --> 00:11:56,323
看，他直接嗖地冲走了！
Look, he's just roaring off!

186
00:11:56,323 --> 00:11:59,311
我这儿装了五升引擎。詹姆斯只有三点五升的。
I've got a five-litre engine here.
James only has three and a half.

187
00:11:59,311 --> 00:12:00,355
不过，他那台有两个涡轮。
Mind you, with two turbos.

188
00:12:03,279 --> 00:12:06,307
奇怪的是，哈蒙德的那台巨大的5.8升V8竟没有出现。
No sign of Hammond, strangely,
with his massive 5.8-litre V8.

189
00:12:09,271 --> 00:12:12,275
哦哟！哦！
Oh-ho! Oh!

190
00:12:12,275 --> 00:12:15,279
那两个人明显在来回挑衅。
Those two are clearly
enjoying a bit of a joust.

191
00:12:15,279 --> 00:12:18,295
杰里米的保时捷配备了被动后轮转向。
Jeremy's Porsche's got passive
rear-wheel steering.

192
00:12:18,295 --> 00:12:19,359
它们都有正经的悬挂系统。
They've both got proper suspension.

193
00:12:19,359 --> 00:12:24,327
我的野马根本没有这些配置，我只能躲着不管，尽量多打方向盘，却只能直线行驶。
I haven't got any of those things
on my Mustang so I'm going to stay

194
00:12:24,327 --> 00:12:28,299
野马还有个问题——油耗极大。
out of it and do a lot of steering,
just to go in a straight line.

195
00:12:30,271 --> 00:12:36,291
不久哈蒙德就得停车加油了。
There was another problem with the
Mustang - it was extremely thirsty.

196
00:12:36,291 --> 00:12:40,287
我和梅在咖啡店等着…
And soon Hammond needed to
stop for fuel.

197
00:12:40,287 --> 00:12:41,367
我喜欢莲花那种著名的操控感、性能……
As May
and I waited in the coffee shop...

198
00:12:41,367 --> 00:12:45,311
哈蒙德加满油了，但从我们坐的地方看，他好像根本没在加油。
I enjoy the things that made Lotus
famous, like steering feel, performance...

199
00:12:45,311 --> 00:12:49,283
根本不像他真的在加油……根本不是金属的。
Hammond filled up but from where
we were sitting, it didn't

200
00:12:49,283 --> 00:12:52,319
look like he was doing that at all.
..not metal.
look like he was doing that at all.
..not metal.

201
00:12:52,319 --> 00:12:56,363
不好意思打断一下，我觉得哈蒙德真是太爱那辆野马了。
Sorry to interrupt but I think
Hammond really loves that Mustang.

202
00:13:05,295 --> 00:13:06,315
他到底在干嘛？
What is he doing?

203
00:13:11,287 --> 00:13:14,287
给这辆肌肉车加满油，
With the muscle car fed,
it looked like we were going to

204
00:13:14,287 --> 00:13:17,327
看起来我们要完成那段130英里简单的挑战。
complete our simple 130-mile
challenge.

205
00:13:20,347 --> 00:13:22,339
是啊。
Yeah.

206
00:13:22,339 --> 00:13:24,287
但随后……
But then...

207
00:13:24,287 --> 00:13:27,291
这是什么……哦！
What's... Ooh!

208
00:13:27,291 --> 00:13:29,279
那烟冒出来了。他在冒烟。
That is smoking. He's smoking.

209
00:13:29,279 --> 00:13:32,323
哈蒙德，你在冒烟，冒得真是够呛。
Hammond, you're smoking,
you're smoking badly.

210
00:13:32,323 --> 00:13:34,287
哦，*（哔——）
Oh, sh... (BLEEP).

211
00:13:34,287 --> 00:13:36,367
我得停下。停下，我的方向盘失灵了。哎呀！
I'm stopping.
I'm stopping. I've lost steering. Oh!

212
00:13:37,367 --> 00:13:41,291
离巴奇还有一英里半……一英里半。
One and a half miles from Butch...
One and a half miles.

213
00:13:41,291 --> 00:13:45,351
……巴奇·卡西迪的老宅。快给我指挥一下。
..Butch Cassidy's house.
Just talk me through it.

214
00:13:45,351 --> 00:13:49,331
动力转向系统，把油全喷了，液体全泄了。
Power steering,
thrown all its oil out, fluid.

215
00:13:49,331 --> 00:13:56,279
那才是冒烟的原因，油在进气歧管上烧掉……我不想听。
That's what was making the smoke, it
was burning off on the manifold...
I'm not interested.

216
00:13:56,279 --> 00:13:59,271
一英里半！
One and a half miles!

217
00:14:02,311 --> 00:14:06,271
是啊，那是量油尺。
Yeah, that's
the dipstick for the fluid.

218
00:14:06,271 --> 00:14:08,323
现在空空如也，油全流光了。
And it's completely empty.
It's all come out.

219
00:14:16,291 --> 00:14:18,283
找到了！
There it is!

220
00:14:20,319 --> 00:14:23,363
天哪！我要留在这里，巴奇曾经住过的地方。
Oh, my God! I'm going to stay here,
where Butch lived.

221
00:14:35,367 --> 00:14:38,343
我把那部电影背得滚瓜烂熟，台词全记住了。
I know that film off by heart.
I know all the lines.

222
00:14:38,343 --> 00:14:40,335
想听我背几句吗？
Would you like to hear some?

223
00:14:40,335 --> 00:14:42,331
不想。
No.

224
00:14:42,331 --> 00:14:45,343
那电影说他在玻利维亚，实际上也真在玻利维亚去世了
The film said it was Bolivia
and he did actually die in Bolivia

225
00:14:45,343 --> 00:14:49,307
但他们在这里找到了他，他又跑了，躲过去了。
but they found him here and he ran
and got away with it again.

226
00:14:49,307 --> 00:14:50,327
行吧。
Right.

227
00:14:50,327 --> 00:14:52,335
我才不在乎它不怎么豪华。
I don't care that it's not
luxurious.

228
00:14:52,335 --> 00:14:58,295
我有自己的枕头，还有巴奇·卡西迪和《日落骑士》嘛。
I've got my own pillow and
Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid.

229
00:15:00,327 --> 00:15:04,275
那扇门大概是他装的。
He probably built that door.

230
00:15:05,359 --> 00:15:07,359
在傍晚的饮酒时光里，
Over an early evening drink,

231
00:15:07,359 --> 00:15:11,367
杰里米仍旧在唠叨他最爱的那个话题。
Jeremy was STILL
going on about his favourite topic.

232
00:15:11,367 --> 00:15:14,343
你不是每周都看吗？不是，我才看呢。
Don't you watch it every week?
No. I do.

233
00:15:14,343 --> 00:15:18,271
《不列颠之战》前五名里，巴奇·卡西迪排名第一，
Battle of Britain's top five
but Butch Cassidy's number one,

234
00:15:18,271 --> 00:15:19,327
《本土英雄》排第二。
Local Hero number two.

235
00:15:19,327 --> 00:15:21,295
《雄鹰敢闯》怎么办？
What about Where Eagles Dare,
though?

236
00:15:21,295 --> 00:15:23,335
不，没上前五。不是吗？不如《不列颠之战》好。
No, not top five. No?
Not as good as Battle of Britain.

237
00:15:23,335 --> 00:15:26,303
不如，不过没有什么能比《不列颠之战》更好。
It's not as good as, but nothing's
as good as Battle of Britain.

238
00:15:26,303 --> 00:15:29,359
它们俩都不如《巴奇·卡西迪与日光...》哦，看看谁来了。
And neither of them are as good as
Butch Cassidy and the Sun... Oh, look who's here.

239
00:15:29,359 --> 00:15:35,283
这倒好。他在逼我。不，不，不，不，不。
That's better.
He's pushing it. No, no, no, no, no.

240
00:15:35,283 --> 00:15:36,351
别，呃……
Don't, er...

241
00:15:36,351 --> 00:15:40,287
各位，诺曼·智慧登场啦。
Norman Wisdom, ladies and gentlemen,
has arrived.

242
00:15:40,287 --> 00:15:42,367
现在他卡住了，懂吧。
Now he's stuck, you know.

243
00:15:42,367 --> 00:15:45,315
哎，车子压到他了，各位，抱歉啊。
Oh, it's run over him,
everybody, I'm sorry.

244
00:15:46,323 --> 00:15:47,363
哦，sh...（哔——）
Oh, sh... (BLEEP).

245
00:15:47,363 --> 00:15:52,275
是啊，所有…制作人说他们会
算作你已经完成了。
Yeah, all r...the producers say they'll
count that as if you've made it.

246
00:15:52,275 --> 00:15:54,279
对，你们也是同一圈子。
Yeah, you're in the same field.

247
00:15:54,279 --> 00:15:56,299
干得好，兄弟。行啊。
Well done, mate. Yeah.

248
00:15:56,299 --> 00:15:58,363
看看你们站哪儿——
巴奇·卡西迪的真房子。
Look where you are -
Butch Cassidy's actual house.

249
00:15:58,363 --> 00:16:00,331
就这儿，真的就这么回事儿？
That is it, genuinely for real?

250
00:16:00,331 --> 00:16:03,323
是啊——你在威尔士也是住这种
地方吗？差不多吧。
Yeah - do you live in something like
that in Wales? Pretty much, yeah.

251
00:16:03,323 --> 00:16:06,351
哦，等下。啥？啥？
Oh, wait a minute. What? What?

252
00:16:06,351 --> 00:16:10,275
啥？我们搞定了。我们到啦。
快点，我快到啦，看这儿。
What? We've done it. We're here.
Come on. I'm nearly here, look.

253
00:16:10,275 --> 00:16:11,315
等一下。
Wait a minute.

254
00:16:11,315 --> 00:16:13,359
呃……
Well...

255
00:16:13,359 --> 00:16:16,295
他们把今天上午给我们的那张
擦掉了
They've crossed out the one
they gave us this morning

256
00:16:16,295 --> 00:16:18,303
又用毛笔写了一张新单子。
and written another one in felt tip.

257
00:16:18,303 --> 00:16:22,307
“你们还没完呢。
明早还有新闻。”
"You haven't finished yet.
More news in the morning."

258
00:16:22,307 --> 00:16:24,283
我们还没结束？
We haven't finished?

259
00:16:24,283 --> 00:16:26,283
还有新闻？
More news?

260
00:16:26,283 --> 00:16:29,323
他们显然发现，还差两个小时的内容。
They've obviously realised that they
haven't filled two hours.

261
00:16:41,351 --> 00:16:42,355
你的软……
Your soft...

262
00:16:45,307 --> 00:16:48,327
……白色……
..white...

263
00:16:48,327 --> 00:16:51,315
……肉！
..flesh.

264
00:16:51,315 --> 00:16:53,331
我的，全是我的！
Mine, all mine!

265
00:17:03,287 --> 00:17:08,271
基本上，我就是保罗·纽曼——
眼睛同色，年纪中年。
Basically, I AM Paul Newman -
same colour eyes, middle aged.

266
00:17:08,271 --> 00:17:09,351
我倒挺享受这个身份的。
I like being this.

267
00:17:12,327 --> 00:17:16,275
你在干什么？
那是巴奇·卡西迪的一个场景。
What are you doing?
It's a scene from Butch Cassidy.

268
00:17:16,275 --> 00:17:18,327
是啊，我知道那段，
但那根本不是自行车，
Yeah, I know that bit
but that's not a bicycle,

269
00:17:18,327 --> 00:17:21,363
他根本不是凯瑟琳·罗斯，
我又拍不好。
he's really not Katharine Ross
and I'm a rubbish shot.

270
00:17:21,363 --> 00:17:25,275
我不…我只是……
我们在巴奇·卡西迪的屋子。
I don't...I'm just having...
we're at Butch Cassidy's house.

271
00:17:25,275 --> 00:17:30,323
哦，就这样。
谢谢，这就是挑战。
Oh, this is it.
Thank you, this is the challenge.

272
00:17:30,323 --> 00:17:32,315
来啊。
Go on.

273
00:17:32,315 --> 00:17:37,271
“现在你们得驱车前往火地岛的乌舒艾亚。”
"You will now drive to Ushuaia
in Tierra del Fuego.

274
00:17:37,271 --> 00:17:40,319
“那是世界最南端的城市，
通往南极的门户”
"It's the southernmost city in
the world, the gateway to Antarctica

275
00:17:40,319 --> 00:17:46,311
“也是南半球文明的最后据点。”
"and the last outpost of
civilisation in the southern hemisphere.

276
00:17:46,311 --> 00:17:50,307
“那里还是‘贝尔格拉诺’战舰的
起航港口，”
"It was also the port from with
the Belgrano, the battleship,

277
00:17:50,307 --> 00:17:55,347
“它在那次宿命航程中出发，
引发了马岛战争的开端。”
"sailed on its fateful voyage
and the start of the Falklands War.

278
00:17:55,347 --> 00:18:00,275
“于是，当地的反英情绪
高涨得很。”
"As a result, anti-British
feelings run high there.

279
00:18:00,275 --> 00:18:04,295
“所以你们得动用外交技巧
来搭起桥梁。”
"So you will use your diplomatic
skills to build bridges."

280
00:18:04,295 --> 00:18:06,347
我们根本没有外交技巧。
We don't have any diplomatic skills.

281
00:18:06,347 --> 00:18:09,307
不，我们倒是会造
桥的，这事儿能搞定。
No, but we're good at building
bridges. We can do that.

282
00:18:09,307 --> 00:18:10,367
不，这只是夸张说法。
No, it's a figure of speech.

283
00:18:10,367 --> 00:18:13,331
它并不是字面上的
建桥。
It doesn't literally mean
build a bridge.

284
00:18:13,331 --> 00:18:14,363
绝对不是。它说，
Absolutely not. It says,

285
00:18:14,363 --> 00:18:18,327
“当你到达乌斯怀亚时，
必须建一个足球场
"When you arrive in Ushuaia,
you must build a football stadium

