00:18:18,327 --> 00:18:22,355
并且和阿根廷球队来场
汽车足球比赛。”
"and host a game of car football
against a team from Argentina."

287
00:18:22,355 --> 00:18:25,339
真的？要用我们的车
来踢汽车足球？
Really? So we're using our cars
in car football?

288
00:18:25,339 --> 00:18:27,339
我的车有点儿大。
Mine's a bit big.

289
00:18:27,339 --> 00:18:31,315
对阵一支队伍，对吧……
在火地岛吗？
Against a team, right...
In Tierra del Fuego?

290
00:18:33,279 --> 00:18:34,311
有多远？
How far is it?

291
00:18:34,311 --> 00:18:35,331
有多远？
How far is it?

292
00:18:35,331 --> 00:18:37,279
一千六百英里。
1,600 miles.

293
00:18:37,279 --> 00:18:39,367
一千六百英里？
One thousand six hundred miles?

294
00:18:41,307 --> 00:18:44,355
坐莲花？
In a Lotus?

295
00:18:46,347 --> 00:18:49,303
在前往南美洲最南端的路上，
On the way to the tip
of South America,

296
00:18:49,303 --> 00:18:54,291
我们这脆弱、年迈、结构复杂的车子
将面对沙漠，
our brittle, ageing,
complicated cars would face deserts,

297
00:18:54,291 --> 00:18:56,295
暴风雪，
blizzards,

298
00:18:56,295 --> 00:18:59,295
积雪堆、泥泞，
snowdrifts, mud,

299
00:18:59,295 --> 00:19:01,283
沼泽，
swamps,

300
00:19:01,283 --> 00:19:04,307
艰苦的山路
以及崎岖的海岸线。
gruelling mountain tracks
and jagged coastlines.

301
00:19:05,343 --> 00:19:07,311
这将是一段史诗级的旅程。
It would be an epic journey.

302
00:19:08,355 --> 00:19:10,307
但在旅程开始之前，
But before it could begin,

303
00:19:10,307 --> 00:19:14,271
哈蒙德得先修好他那野马的
助力转向，
Hammond had to mend his Mustang's
power steering,

304
00:19:14,271 --> 00:19:16,295
这就给了我点儿消磨时间的机会。
which meant I had time to kill.

305
00:19:21,275 --> 00:19:25,275
# 雨点不停砸在我头上
# Raindrops keep falling on my head

306
00:19:25,275 --> 00:19:30,363
# 就像那个人的
脚大到床都装不下
# And just like a guy whose
feet are too big for his bed

307
00:19:30,363 --> 00:19:34,347
# 没有什么能适应
这些雨点…… #
# Nothing seems to fit
those raindrops... #

308
00:19:34,347 --> 00:19:37,271
他还在坚持吗？嗯。
Is he still doing it? Mhm.

309
00:19:37,271 --> 00:19:39,271
好吧。不会出现的。
OK. It won't have it.

310
00:19:41,275 --> 00:19:43,291
其实，我还记得影片里
有这么一段，
Actually, I do remember this
bit in the film,

311
00:19:43,291 --> 00:19:46,283
保罗·纽曼骑着自行车四处转，
不是吗？对。
because Paul Newman rides around on
the bicycle, doesn't he? Yeah.

312
00:19:46,283 --> 00:19:49,295
接着凯瑟琳·罗斯
甜甜地笑出声“哈哈哈！”
And then Katharine Ross does
a little playful "ha-ha-ha!" giggle

313
00:19:49,295 --> 00:19:52,303
还往他脸上扔点稻草。
对吧？对。对。
and throws some straw in his face.
Yeah. Is that right? Yeah. Yeah.

314
00:19:52,303 --> 00:19:59,271
# 那些雨点正砸在我头上，
它们不停地掉下来
# Those raindrops are falling
on my head, they keep falling

315
00:19:59,271 --> 00:20:01,331
# 因为我自由…… #
# Because I'm free... #

316
00:20:01,331 --> 00:20:04,331
哎哟！
Ow!

317
00:20:04,331 --> 00:20:07,367
在我们和杰里米把
助力转向弄得乱七八糟后，
After we'd dealt with Jeremy
and bodged the power steering,

318
00:20:07,367 --> 00:20:09,359
我们朝南出发。
we headed south.

319
00:20:16,355 --> 00:20:21,331
莲花Esprit V8
是进行一千六百英里奔驰的好选择吗
Is the Lotus Esprit V8 a good
choice for a 1,600-mile drive

320
00:20:21,331 --> 00:20:23,303
穿越巴塔哥尼亚吗？
through Patagonia?

321
00:20:23,303 --> 00:20:24,323
说实话，不会。
In all honesty, no.

322
00:20:26,287 --> 00:20:29,291
但是——我自己在想，观众们想知道——
But - and the question I'm asking
myself, viewers is -

323
00:20:29,291 --> 00:20:31,315
哈蒙德的野马能顶住吗？
will Hammond's Mustang make it?

324
00:20:31,315 --> 00:20:34,291
我说不清楚，但每次站在老车旁边，
And I can't really explain this
but when I stand near an old car,

325
00:20:34,291 --> 00:20:36,335
我都会有种预感，觉得它挺好，
I get a feeling
when I know it's a good one,

326
00:20:36,335 --> 00:20:39,355
但哈蒙德的野马我一点感觉都没有。
and I'm not getting that feeling
with Hammond's Mustang.

327
00:20:39,355 --> 00:20:41,335
看起来就像是挂在半空。
It feels like it's hanging on.

328
00:20:41,335 --> 00:20:43,367
哎呀，我的安全带又散架了。
Oh, no!
My seat belt's fallen apart again.

329
00:20:50,271 --> 00:20:53,343
为了到达目的地，我们决定去智利
To reach our destination,
we decided to head into Chile

330
00:20:53,343 --> 00:20:58,283
顺便拎起听起来很重要的《通往南方之路》。
and pick up the important-sounding
Road To The South.

331
00:20:58,283 --> 00:20:59,347
这就得穿越安第斯山脉，
This meant crossing the Andes,

332
00:20:59,347 --> 00:21:04,303
听起来够复杂的，我就自告奋勇了。
and as that sounded complicated,
I put myself in charge.

333
00:21:04,303 --> 00:21:07,315
想想看，要是我们得跨安第斯山，
Well, it strikes me that if we've
got to cross the Andes,

334
00:21:07,315 --> 00:21:10,323
那就该在这里过，而不是往更南边走，
we should do that here
rather than further south,

335
00:21:10,323 --> 00:21:12,323
因为这儿的雪会少点。
cos there'll be less snow here.

336
00:21:12,323 --> 00:21:15,339
好啊，听起来更靠谱吧？
Right, that's a better idea, is it?

337
00:21:15,339 --> 00:21:18,351
太妙了，我们就……在这儿跨过去。
It's a brilliant idea so we shall...
We'll cross them up here.

338
00:21:22,363 --> 00:21:24,363
起初，我的计划进行得顺利。
At first, my plan went well.

339
00:21:33,291 --> 00:21:38,287
这条路简直让人目不转睛。
This road is simply mesmerizing.

340
00:21:43,355 --> 00:21:49,311
我们甚至想出了在野马不停加油时自娱自乐的办法。
We even found a way to amuse ourselves
during the Mustang's endless fuel stops.

341
00:21:57,363 --> 00:22:02,295
看这表情。
Look at this face.

342
00:22:02,295 --> 00:22:04,363
# 来上吧
# Let's get it on

343
00:22:04,363 --> 00:22:06,367
# 来爱吧，宝宝
# Let's love, baby

344
00:22:08,307 --> 00:22:13,307
# 来上吧，甜心
# Let's get it on
Sugar

345
00:22:13,307 --> 00:22:18,311
# 来上吧。#
# Let's get it on. #

346
00:22:20,295 --> 00:22:24,355
出发后我们才发现老是停下来是怎么回事。
After we set off we discovered why
we kept having to stop.

347
00:22:24,355 --> 00:22:27,303
哈蒙德！什么？
Hammond! What?

348
00:22:27,303 --> 00:22:29,287
只要踩到底就行。
Just put your foot down hard.

349
00:22:30,367 --> 00:22:35,279
嗯，我大概知道你油耗这么糙的原因了。
Yeah, I think I know why your fuel
consumption's quite poor.

350
00:22:39,295 --> 00:22:42,327
福克兰群岛的地图上写着“阿根廷永远拥有”。
Map of the Falkland Islands with
"Argentina's forever."

351
00:22:44,351 --> 00:22:49,339
我现在是一脸正经，真的正经。
That is a straight face
I'm pulling right now, straight.

352
00:22:49,339 --> 00:22:52,355
这趟我不想挑起什么争端。
I will not spark fury on this trip.

353
00:22:52,355 --> 00:22:55,319
这就是全新我，聪明的我，机灵的我。
This is the new me,
the smart me, the clever me.

354
00:22:58,359 --> 00:23:02,279
不久后，我选的路况变差了点。
Soon, the road I'd chosen
got a bit worse.

355
00:23:05,275 --> 00:23:07,283
哔——。
BLEEP.

356
00:23:08,299 --> 00:23:11,283
哦，哦，哦。
Oh, oh, oh.

357
00:23:12,355 --> 00:23:14,347
哎呀，天哪！
Ah, God!

358
00:23:14,347 --> 00:23:18,315
嘿，克拉克森，你是说从阿根廷开到智利这条是主路？我才不信。
Oi, Clarkson, are you telling me
that if you drive from Argentina to Chile

359
00:23:18,315 --> 00:23:20,339
ON RADIO: 是的，的确是。
this is the main road?
Cos I don't believe it.

360
00:23:20,339 --> 00:23:23,291
ON RADIO: Yes, it is.
ON RADIO: Yes, it is.

361
00:23:23,291 --> 00:23:25,275
这不就说明了嘛，真的，
Just goes to show, doesn't it,
really,

362
00:23:25,275 --> 00:23:27,315
关于汽车有多牛逼，因为……
about how brilliant cars are,
because...

363
00:23:38,271 --> 00:23:40,343
结果路一下子全没了。
And then the road disappeared
altogether.

364
00:23:44,287 --> 00:23:45,315
哦，天啊。
Oh, Lord.

365
00:23:48,299 --> 00:23:51,283
这车子可不适合这么玩。
Which wasn't ideal
in cars like these.

366
00:23:53,307 --> 00:23:54,363
詹姆斯，我们真是蠢材，
James, we're the idiots,

367
00:23:54,363 --> 00:23:58,339
我们居然听他建议走那条路线。
we listened to him
with a suggestion for a route.

368
00:23:58,339 --> 00:24:00,347
放轻松，我们快到了。
Relax, we're nearly there now.

369
00:24:05,367 --> 00:24:09,311
哎呦。哎呦。
Ow. Ow.

370
00:24:09,311 --> 00:24:12,279
哦！奇怪的声音！
Oh! Bad noises!

371
00:24:14,299 --> 00:24:17,275
我也不知道该咋办——继续走克拉克森那条蠢路，
I don't know what's best - keep
going on Clarkson's stupid route,

372
00:24:17,275 --> 00:24:18,363
还是掉头回去找别的路。
turn round and go back
and find another one.

373
00:24:21,303 --> 00:24:24,339
哦！哦！
Oh! Oh!

374
00:24:24,339 --> 00:24:26,311
哎呀，糟了。
Oh, dear.

375
00:24:33,311 --> 00:24:35,319
哔——。
BLEEP.

376
00:24:35,319 --> 00:24:38,363
哦，见鬼的。调好诺拉！
Oh, bloody hell.
Cocking Nora!

377
00:24:43,367 --> 00:24:45,359
你怎么能不喜欢这条路？
How can you not like this road?

378
00:24:45,359 --> 00:24:47,355
别闹了，这路真是太棒了。
Go away. It's brilliant.

379
00:24:49,367 --> 00:24:52,347
然后，不出所料……
And then, inevitably...

380
00:24:52,347 --> 00:24:55,343
哦！哦，我失去方向盘了。
Oh! Oh, I've lost steering.

381
00:25:00,307 --> 00:25:02,299
把詹姆斯救了之后……
Having rescued James...

382
00:25:03,367 --> 00:25:05,343
耶——！
Ya-hey!

383
00:25:05,343 --> 00:25:07,359
……我们决定把哈蒙德丢下，
..we decided to leave Hammond,

384
00:25:07,359 --> 00:25:12,275
虽然很快离开了森林，但仍旧身陷困境。
and though we were soon out the
woods, we weren't out of the woods.

385
00:25:13,299 --> 00:25:14,315
哎呀……
Oh, my...

386
00:25:15,335 --> 00:25:19,319
来吧，别现在掉链子啊，小保时捷。
Come on, don't let me down now,
little Porsche.

387
00:25:25,351 --> 00:25:28,355
这儿，莲花完全跑出了它的舒适区。
Here, the Lotus was way
out of its comfort zone.

388
00:25:32,343 --> 00:25:34,275
啊！
Ah!

389
00:25:35,359 --> 00:25:38,343
不过，神奇的是，它竟然成功了。
But, amazingly, it made it.

390
00:25:40,355 --> 00:25:44,319
我真是惊讶得不行，莲花居然还能跑。
I am absolutely staggered that Lotus
is still working.

391
00:25:44,319 --> 00:25:47,295
绝对是，彻底惊掉下巴。
Absolutely, properly staggered.

392
00:25:49,319 --> 00:25:53,367
好吧，是啊，我真想说那玩得真爽……
Well, yeah, I'd love to be able to
say that was great fun...

393
00:25:57,295 --> 00:26:01,303
不久后，我和詹姆斯来到了智利边境。
Shortly afterwards, James and I
arrived at the Chilean border.

394
00:26:01,303 --> 00:26:04,331
我早就看好穿越安第斯的这条路，果然不赖。
I knew my route across the Andes
would be good, and it is.

395
00:26:06,315 --> 00:26:11,307
把他方向盘的临时补丁改好后，哈蒙德也赶紧上路了。
And having bodged the bodge on his
steering, Hammond, too, was on the move.

396
00:26:11,307 --> 00:26:15,311
但其他的毛病也开始冒出来了。
But other gremlins were
starting to appear.

397
00:26:15,311 --> 00:26:17,319
我的天啊，我丢了三挡。
Oh, my God. I've lost third gear.

398
00:26:19,331 --> 00:26:22,335
于是，他在边境哨所打了个盹，
So, as he caught 40 winks
at the border post,

399
00:26:22,335 --> 00:26:25,307
我和梅决定给他打打气。
May and I decided to cheer him up.

400
00:26:25,307 --> 00:26:28,331
别再往后倒了，别急。
Don't pull any more
backing off yet.

401
00:26:41,307 --> 00:26:44,299
什么？为什么……？你为什么要把它装在我车上？
What? Why...? Why have you
put that on my car?

402
00:26:47,367 --> 00:26:51,271
在智利，哈蒙德对我们的表现并不满意。
In Chile, Hammond was not
impressed with our efforts.

403
00:26:52,299 --> 00:26:54,335
哈蒙德，你的标致怎么样？
How's your Peugeot, Hammond?

404
00:26:54,335 --> 00:26:56,311
闭嘴。
Shut up.

405
00:26:56,311 --> 00:27:00,307
我基本上给它贴了标致的贴纸，想让它更可靠点。
I've basically put Peugeot stickers
on it to try and make it more reliable.

406
00:27:00,307 --> 00:27:02,331
可惜，根本没起作用。
Sadly, though, that didn't work.

407
00:27:03,335 --> 00:27:04,363
哦，不。哦，不。
Oh, no. Oh, no.

408
00:27:04,363 --> 00:27:09,307
我不想说，但我又失去动力转向了。
I hate to say this -
I've lost power steering again.

409
00:27:09,307 --> 00:27:11,347
他们笑
THEY LAUGH

410
00:27:13,295 --> 00:27:17,307
再一次把哈蒙德甩在身后，我和詹姆斯决定好好享受这条路
Leaving Hammond once more, James
and I decided to enjoy a road

411
00:27:17,307 --> 00:27:23,299
这条路本可以专门为我们这匹经过细致调校的欧洲跑马打造。
that could have been purpose built for
our finely-turned European thoroughbreds.

412
00:27:28,287 --> 00:27:31,311
哦，哇！这儿的方向盘手感太棒了。
Oh, wow!
The feel through the steering, here.

413
00:27:34,363 --> 00:27:38,347
进弯时，感受前轮把肩部压进弯道。
Into the corner, feel the front,
shoving its shoulder into the job.

414
00:27:40,271 --> 00:27:43,295
我们现在都忘记了车子过去有多好。
We forget these days how good
cars used to be.

415
00:27:43,295 --> 00:27:46,307
不在安全上，不在燃油经济性上，也不在排放上，
Not at safety, not at fuel economy,
not at emissions,

416
00:27:46,307 --> 00:27:49,363
只在驾驭乐趣，只在操控感上。
just joy, just handling.

417
00:27:51,367 --> 00:27:54,299
我完全相信，我现在玩得更嗨
I'm absolutely confident
I am now having a better time

418
00:27:54,299 --> 00:27:58,295
因为我坐在专为这种事儿设计的车上，它是中置发动机。
because I'm in the car designed
for this sort of thing. It's mid-engined.

419
00:27:58,295 --> 00:28:01,323
当然啦，坐中置发动机的车，酷得不行。
And, of course, if you have a
mid-engined car, it looks cool.

420
00:28:05,315 --> 00:28:07,343
哦，哔——！
Oh, BLEEP!

421
00:28:10,311 --> 00:28:11,347
耶稣哭了！
Jesus wept!

422
00:28:11,347 --> 00:28:13,359
是啊。
Yes.

423
00:28:13,359 --> 00:28:17,363
我刚才演示的其实是中置发动机论点的另一面，
What I was just demonstrating
there was the other side of
the mid-engined argument,

424
00:28:17,363 --> 00:28:21,291
也就是说，它一发动，冲得更快一点。
which is, when it does go it,
it goes a bit more quickly.

425
00:28:21,291 --> 00:28:24,327
他现在就会坐在自己粪便里。
He'll now be sitting up to here
in his own excrement.

426
00:28:27,343 --> 00:28:29,351
尽管如此，我们还是继续前进，
Despite this, though, we pressed on,

427
00:28:29,351 --> 00:28:35,271
大快朵颐地享受我们来这里的根本——引擎的魅力。
savouring the whole point
of our being here - our engines.

428
00:28:35,271 --> 00:28:37,347
听这声音，奇特的 V8 发出的低沉咆哮。
Listen to that, the grumble
of an offbeat V8.

429
00:28:43,271 --> 00:28:46,279
我把挡位降到二档，让你听到真正的咆哮。
I'll knock it down to second
so you can hear the proper roar.

430
00:28:46,279 --> 00:28:47,351
听好了。
Listen to that.

431
00:28:54,287 --> 00:29:00,307
到了下一座城镇，我们把车拦下来，聊起 V8 那点儿 ‘nerd’ 的魅力所在。
In the next town, we pulled over
for a nerdy chat about what makes
a V8 so special.

432
00:29:00,307 --> 00:29:05,295
它是一台有魅力的发动机，这也是我们爱 V8 的原因，因为它们本身就不完美。
It is a charismatic engine,
that's why we like V8s, is cos
they are imperfect.

433
00:29:05,295 --> 00:29:06,299
是的，非常。
Yes, very.

434
00:29:06,299 --> 00:29:10,291
不像直列六缸发动机，六个气缸排成一条直线，
Unlike a straight six engine, where
you've got six cylinders in line,

435
00:29:10,291 --> 00:29:14,271
在那种布局里，一个活塞往下时，另一个正往上冲，
in one of those, when one piston's
going down another one's coming up,

436
00:29:14,271 --> 00:29:17,287
于是它自己相互平衡，运转得很平顺。是啊。
so it sort of balances
itself and makes it smooth. Yes.

437
00:29:17,287 --> 00:29:20,331
而 V8 天生不平衡，因为当一个活塞下行时，
A V8 is inherently unbalanced,
because when one piston's going down,

438
00:29:20,331 --> 00:29:23,311
不一定会有另一个活塞上行来平衡它。
there isn't necessarily
another one going up to balance it.

439
00:29:23,311 --> 00:29:26,343
没错，而且它们的运动方向也不相同，因为…
Exactly, and they're not going in
the same direction, are they, cos...

440
00:29:26,343 --> 00:29:31,355
是啊，正是如此，这就是 V8 抖动的根源。
Yeah, exactly, so they're sort of doing that.
So that's what makes a V8 wobbly.

441
00:29:31,355 --> 00:29:35,339
它啊，本来就摇摇晃晃的。
还带点儿魅力，没错。
It is, it's inherently wobbly.
And charismatic. Yes.

442
00:29:35,339 --> 00:29:38,307
不过你车里的V8
可不一样，对吧？
But the V8 in your car
isn't the same, is it?

443
00:29:38,307 --> 00:29:42,275
因为，老实说，
我从没想过会在《Top Gear》里说出这些话，
Because, and I never thought
I would use these words on Top Gear,

444
00:29:42,275 --> 00:29:44,347
它用了平面曲轴。
it has a flat plane crank.

445
00:29:44,347 --> 00:29:46,327
很好，正是如此。
Very good. Exactly.

446
00:29:46,327 --> 00:29:49,295
在你那辆里，
发动机的汽缸走向……
In yours,
the engine cylinders they go...

447
00:29:50,335 --> 00:29:54,291
..于是两个气缸会在同一边点火
而我这边，却是……
..so you get two firing
on the same side. Mine just goes...

448
00:29:54,291 --> 00:29:59,331
所以，你那台像查理·沃茨那样，
而另一台V8，我的，
So, yours is like Charlie Watts,
and the other V8, mine,

449
00:29:59,331 --> 00:30:02,331
更像基思·穆恩。
还有点儿意思。
is more Keith Moon.
There's a bit more going on.

450
00:30:02,331 --> 00:30:04,327
是啊，这才是区别所在。
Yes, and that's what makes
the difference.

451
00:30:04,327 --> 00:30:07,319
这就是传统V8——
也就是美式V8的原因，
That's why traditional V8s -
i.e., the American style V8,

452
00:30:07,319 --> 00:30:10,319
大概就是你那台的风格，
它们只会嗡嗡响，我这台却是咆哮。
which is sort of what yours is,
they burble, but mine snarls.

453
00:30:10,319 --> 00:30:14,343
我们的同事随后出现了，
把自己的烂摊子又弄得更烂。
Our colleague then turned up having
bodged the bodge of his bodge.

454
00:30:20,291 --> 00:30:23,323
修好？嗯。
好，走起！
Fixed? Yeah.
Right, let's go!

455
00:30:23,323 --> 00:30:27,347
咖啡不错吧？嗯，真的很棒。
味儿好极了。好！
Coffee good? Yeah, it was lovely.
It was delicious. Good!

456
00:30:30,307 --> 00:30:33,303
杰里米·克拉克森，詹姆斯·梅。
Jeremy Clarkson, James May.

457
00:30:33,303 --> 00:30:34,367
是啊，怎么了？
Yes, what's wrong?

458
00:30:34,367 --> 00:30:38,319
呃，我刚在想要不要
给房子再抵押，心里纠结着
Uh, I was just thinking of
remortgaging my house and wondering

459
00:30:38,319 --> 00:30:42,299
到底是选固定利率还是浮动政策，你们觉得呢？
if I should go for a fixed rate or
a flexible policy, what do you think?

460
00:30:42,299 --> 00:30:47,343
你们也清楚，商界人士
可开不了这种车，
As you well know, businessmen
do not drive cars of this nature,

461
00:30:47,343 --> 00:30:50,335
去年萝卜收成咋样？
how was the turnip harvest
last year?

462
00:30:50,335 --> 00:30:53,319
骂诺福克人倒是挺痛快，
It's all very well being rude
about the people of Norfolk,

463
00:30:53,319 --> 00:30:55,347
但截至目前，他们居然造出了最好的车。
but so far they seem to have
built the best car.

464
00:30:55,347 --> 00:30:59,367
它一点儿毛病也没有，能越野，
而且我闹出乌龙时它救了我。
It hasn't gone wrong, it goes off road and
it saved me when I made a cock-up.

465
00:31:01,307 --> 00:31:07,331
我们沿着杰里米那条蠢路
一直开到这里。
We continued on Jeremy's idiotic
route until we reached this.

466
00:31:07,331 --> 00:31:09,347
我的天啊！
Oh, my God!

467
00:31:11,275 --> 00:31:13,271
这玩意是给车的吗？
Is this for cars?

468
00:31:13,271 --> 00:31:16,311
那就快下车赶紧去，
詹姆斯，去看看到底是啥。
Well, get out and have a jump on it,
James, and go to see if it is.

469
00:31:16,311 --> 00:31:19,351
好，这能让我们
搞清楚一切，等一下。
OK, that will tell us
everything we need to know, hang on.

470
00:31:20,363 --> 00:31:23,339
我的天啊！不对，詹姆斯那是……
等会儿！
Oh, my God! No, James that is...
Oh, hang on a minute!

471
00:31:23,339 --> 00:31:27,339
哎呀，晃晃的！
我说，快看！
Oh, it's wobbly!
I mean, look!

472
00:31:27,339 --> 00:31:29,295
简直烂透了。
It's rubbish.

473
00:31:29,295 --> 00:31:31,279
那根本不是……
That is not...

474
00:31:31,279 --> 00:31:32,319
是一座人行天桥。
It's a footbridge.

475
00:31:32,319 --> 00:31:35,347
我们要么认输，
然后把节目在这里结束。
We either admit defeat
and end the programme here.

476
00:31:35,347 --> 00:31:37,319
好啊，我支持结束。再见。
Well, I'm for ending. Goodbye.

477
00:31:37,319 --> 00:31:39,287
而且这劲爆的消息……！
And on that bombshell...!

478
00:31:40,287 --> 00:31:41,295
走吧！
Come on!

479
00:31:43,271 --> 00:31:46,303
既然詹姆斯抢先了，
他就先上场。
Since James was on point,
he went first.

480
00:31:47,323 --> 00:31:49,275
我们开始吧。
Here we go.

481
00:31:50,315 --> 00:31:53,367
哎呀，天哪，它在下垂！
它动了！哎呀！
Oh, God it's sagging!
It moves! Oh!

482
00:31:53,367 --> 00:31:57,295
别看，别看，
别看，别看。
Not looking, not looking,
not looking, not looking.

483
00:31:57,295 --> 00:31:59,359
天啊，真的让人毛骨悚然！
God, that's really disconcerting!

484
00:32:01,327 --> 00:32:03,347
我表现得怎么样，我表现得怎么样？
How am I doing, how am I doing?

485
00:32:08,327 --> 00:32:11,351
好嘞，来吧。速度！
Right, here we go. Speed!

486
00:32:15,323 --> 00:32:18,299
耶！速度解决了问题。
Yeah! Speed has solved the problem.

487
00:32:19,347 --> 00:32:21,351
这到底是怎么回事？
What the hell?

488
00:32:26,323 --> 00:32:28,323
这是死胡同。我知道。
It's a dead end. I know.

489
00:32:28,323 --> 00:32:29,363
那你怎么不早说？
Well, why didn't you tell me?

490
00:32:29,363 --> 00:32:31,359
因为我想看你撞桥的瞬间。
Cos I wanted to see you
come across the bridge.

491
00:32:36,287 --> 00:32:38,359
我知道你在想啥。
要不要开始？
I know what you're thinking.
Shall we?

492
00:32:38,359 --> 00:32:40,299
来吧，哈蒙德！
Right, come on Hammond!

493
00:32:42,307 --> 00:32:44,327
我的车最重，废话不多说。
My car's the heaviest. Enough said.

494
00:32:47,359 --> 00:32:51,283
别系安全带，免得车掉下来把我卡住。
要是掉下去就别想被困在里面了。
No seatbelt, don't want to be
stuck in it, if it falls off.

495
00:32:58,311 --> 00:32:59,339
哦！
Oh!

496
00:33:01,327 --> 00:33:03,271
哦！
Oh!

497
00:33:04,343 --> 00:33:06,355
我不喜欢，我不喜欢。
I don't like it, I don't like it.

498
00:33:06,355 --> 00:33:09,323
感觉自己在逃离一场灾难。
it feels like I'm running away
from a disaster.

499
00:33:14,323 --> 00:33:17,311
我完成了，我完成了，我完成了。
来点坏消息吧。
I did it, I did it, I did it.
Got some bad news.

500
00:33:17,311 --> 00:33:18,331
什么？是死胡同。
What? It's a dead end.

501
00:33:20,343 --> 00:33:24,347
我们……我们想提醒你，但就是说不出口。
We... We tried to tell you, but we
just couldn't get the message across.

502
00:33:26,303 --> 00:33:30,271
我们开车回去穿过那条针织毛衣桥…
We drove back across the
knit-one-purl-one bridge...

503
00:33:32,303 --> 00:33:35,319
…结果恰好走进雨季
..and found ourselves
in the rainy season

504
00:33:35,319 --> 00:33:38,311
看起来像是《侏罗纪公园》的拍摄现场。
on what appeared to be
the set of Jurassic Park.

505
00:33:44,359 --> 00:33:47,367
石化森林，神秘湖泊，
Petrified forests, mysterious lakes,

506
00:33:47,367 --> 00:33:49,331
这一切都怪怪的。
this is all very odd.

507
00:33:51,351 --> 00:33:54,323
如果我转个弯，看到一只雷龙，
If I go round the next corner
and there's a brontosaurus,

508
00:33:54,323 --> 00:33:56,343
我也不会惊讶。
I will not be surprised.

509
00:34:00,367 --> 00:34:03,355
我不确定这是不是通往南方的路。
I'm not sure this is the road
to the south.

510
00:34:06,343 --> 00:34:09,351
什么时候我们该承认这玩意儿行不通，
When do we just accept
this is not working,

511
00:34:09,351 --> 00:34:12,331
这不对，这不是办法。
this is not right,
this is not the way.

512
00:34:12,331 --> 00:34:16,327
不久赛道把我们带进了原始沼泽。
Soon the track led us
into a primordial swamp.

513
00:34:20,283 --> 00:34:22,283
哎呀，真是气炸了！
Oh, for crying out loud!

514
00:34:22,283 --> 00:34:25,299
这可是928保时捷，天哪！
It's a 928 Porsche,
for heaven's sake!

515
00:34:27,327 --> 00:34:29,275
噢，真是糟透了。
Oh, that felt bad.

516
00:34:31,295 --> 00:34:35,359
要是你是智利人，也许想写封信说，“不，你走错路了。”
If you're Chilean, perhaps
you'd like to write in and say,
"No, you went the wrong way."

517
00:34:37,307 --> 00:34:40,311
不，我卡住了，我要在这儿死了，
No, that's it, I'm stuck,
and I'm going to die here,

518
00:34:40,311 --> 00:34:43,311
孤独而丑陋的死亡。
a lonely, hideous death.

519
00:34:45,283 --> 00:34:46,335
噢，不！
Oh, no!

520
00:34:47,347 --> 00:34:50,363
我和杰里米现在彻底搁浅了。
Jeremy and I were now completely
beached.

521
00:34:52,347 --> 00:34:53,351
不过……
However...

522
00:34:55,323 --> 00:34:59,359
这车简直神了。  
真的神得不行。
This car is incredible.
It is truly incredible.

523
00:34:59,359 --> 00:35:02,343
要是我给你看张这车的图，然后问你，  
‘这玩意儿有什么用？’
If I showed you a picture of this
and said, "what's that good for?"

524
00:35:02,343 --> 00:35:06,359
你肯定会说，‘哦，我才不想把它开进超市停车场，  
那里全是减速带。’
You'd say, "Oh, I wouldn't want to
take that into a supermarket car
park, they've got speed humps."

525
00:35:10,363 --> 00:35:12,355
诺福克来了，拯救局面。
Here comes Norfolk to the rescue.

526
00:35:17,315 --> 00:35:20,323
来啊，杰里米。好！
Come on, Jeremy. Yes!

527
00:35:20,323 --> 00:35:24,299
来啊，保时捷。好，好车！
Come on, Porsche.
Yes, you good, good car.

528
00:35:25,335 --> 00:35:29,299
不想让那惊艳的莲花抢尽风头，
Desperate for the astonishing Lotus
not to hog all the glory,

529
00:35:29,299 --> 00:35:32,359
我决定让保时捷把野马拉起来。
I decided the Porsche would get
the Mustang moving.

530
00:35:32,359 --> 00:35:35,347
国际救援队要来救哈蒙德。
International Rescue is coming
to Hammond's aid.

531
00:35:36,351 --> 00:35:39,347
好，准备好了吗？准备好了。
Right, are you ready?
Yes, I am.

532
00:35:39,347 --> 00:35:44,347
我要数到三、二、一，开始推！
I'm going to start pushing in
three, two, one, go.

533
00:35:53,279 --> 00:35:54,327
我们俩卡住了。
We're both stuck, now.

534
00:35:57,363 --> 00:36:00,367
看看这车！它就是这么晃悠。
Look at it!
It's just driving around.

535
00:36:02,343 --> 00:36:04,311
出点小岔子了？
Having a spot of bother?

536
00:36:05,331 --> 00:36:09,275
它那自豪的美国屁股卡在岩石上。
Its proud American ass
is stuck on a rock.

537
00:36:09,275 --> 00:36:10,359
这屎油屁股。
Its lardy arse.

538
00:36:10,359 --> 00:36:13,271
是啊，这活儿对它有点儿重。
Yes. It's a bit heavy for this
sort of work.

539
00:36:13,271 --> 00:36:16,351
好吧，你说得对，它确实……哦。
Well, you're right, it is...
Oh.

540
00:36:16,351 --> 00:36:18,331
啥？
What?

541
00:36:18,331 --> 00:36:21,291
这玩意儿到底是啥？是2CV皮卡吗？
What the hell is that?
What is it, a 2CV pick-up?

542
00:36:21,291 --> 00:36:25,319
前面像2CV，那后面到底是什么？
Well, it's a 2CV at the front,
then what is it?

543
00:36:25,319 --> 00:36:29,315
我在巴里洛切见过那车。你不可能真的去……
I saw that car in Bariloche.
You can't have done.

544
00:36:29,315 --> 00:36:32,291
那种车。根本不可能是同一辆……
One like it.
It can't possibly be the same one.

545
00:36:36,359 --> 00:36:40,319
总算，哈蒙德和我摆脱了困境。
Finally, Hammond and I
managed to get free.

546
00:36:40,319 --> 00:36:42,331
耶！
Yes!

547
00:36:42,331 --> 00:36:44,299
然后……
And then...

548
00:36:44,299 --> 00:36:47,339
看，那儿就是通往南边的路。
There it is, there's the road to
the south.

549
00:36:47,339 --> 00:36:53,303
瞧——这就是我们一直在找的路，总算找到了。
look - that is what we have been
looking for, and we've found it.

550
00:36:54,347 --> 00:36:59,359
我们和那路之间有条河，但还有座桥。
There was a river between us
and it, but there was also a bridge.

551
00:37:10,363 --> 00:37:15,295
我们离南边的路只有五十米了。
We're now just 50 metres
from the road to the south.

552
00:37:17,355 --> 00:37:19,275
把诺拉搞起来！
Cocking Nora!

553
00:37:20,291 --> 00:37:22,359
怎么了，你这笨蛋？
What's the matter, you idiot?

554
00:37:22,359 --> 00:37:25,347
还没完呢。啊。
It's not finished. Ah.

555
00:37:31,303 --> 00:37:34,299
为什么只造桥的一半？他们到底想干嘛……？
Why would you build part of a bridge?
Why have they built...?

556
00:37:34,299 --> 00:37:36,323
它……它只有九成。看看这。
It's... It's nine tenths.
Look at that.

557
00:37:39,351 --> 00:37:43,291
准备，稳住，抬！
Ready, steady, heave.

558
00:37:43,291 --> 00:37:45,347
不，这玩意儿真重。
No, it's really heavy.

559
00:37:45,347 --> 00:37:49,295
好呀。我们干脆叫摄制组帮忙吧？
Right. Yeah. Why don't we just
get the film crew to help?

560
00:37:49,295 --> 00:37:50,367
摄制组有几百个人呢。
There's hundreds of them.

561
00:37:50,367 --> 00:37:52,319
兄弟们，能不能…？
Guys, can we have...?

562
00:37:56,287 --> 00:37:59,343
稍后不久，我们三个人把桥搞定了。
A short while later, the three of us
had got the bridge finished.

563
00:38:02,359 --> 00:38:06,347
这可是值得自豪的时刻，哈蒙德，不过…
That is a proud moment, Hammond,
but...

564
00:38:06,347 --> 00:38:09,311
它直吗？
is it straight?

565
00:38:09,311 --> 00:38:11,335
对。对。
Yes. Yes.

566
00:38:14,283 --> 00:38:17,355
各位，我就要飞过去了，你们有什么想说的么？
Gentlemen, I'm about to go over
the edge, is there anything you
want to say to me?

567
00:38:17,355 --> 00:38:19,311
能把你的法拉利借给我吗？
Can I have your Ferrari?

568
00:38:22,279 --> 00:38:23,295
哦，他上场了。
Oh, here he goes.

569
00:38:27,311 --> 00:38:29,359
来吧。
Come on.

570
00:38:31,335 --> 00:38:35,355
他搞定啦，面对风险也赢了。
He's done it.
He's faced the peril and won.

571
00:38:38,315 --> 00:38:40,359
其实我们大家都做到了。
In fact, we all did.

572
00:38:40,359 --> 00:38:43,311
哦！来了！
Oh! There it is!

573
00:38:44,311 --> 00:38:47,323
终于，我们上了“通往南方之路”。
And at last,
we were on the Road To The South.

574
00:38:47,323 --> 00:38:51,271
哈哈哈！
Ha ha ha!

575
00:38:58,323 --> 00:39:01,291
第二天早上，我们好心情出发…
The next morning,
we set off in good spirits...

576
00:39:03,351 --> 00:39:06,299
…因为一路顺畅，心情大好。
..overjoyed that the going
was smooth.

577
00:39:07,343 --> 00:39:11,271
沥青路面。哎，真是松了一口气。
Tarmac. Oh, the relief.

578
00:39:12,319 --> 00:39:15,319
可惜的是，才走了半英里…
Sadly, though,
after just half a mile...

579
00:39:17,335 --> 00:39:20,367
天呐！坏消息，哈蒙德。
Oh, God Almighty! Bad news, Hammond.

580
00:39:22,295 --> 00:39:25,279
哎哟！
Ow!

581
00:39:25,279 --> 00:39:29,319
哎哟，哎哟，哎哟！哎！啊！啊！
Ow, ow, ow! Ow! Ah! Ah!

582
00:39:29,319 --> 00:39:34,295
这直接导致那永远闹麻烦的野马轮胎爆了。
This immediately caused the
ever-troublesome Mustang to have a puncture.

583
00:39:38,271 --> 00:39:40,311
詹姆斯，你想等他还是…？
James, do you want to wait for him
or...?

584
00:39:40,311 --> 00:39:43,323
嗯，你知道的，在这种情况下，我觉得公平起见…
Well, do you know, under the circumstances,
I think it would be fair to...

585
00:39:43,323 --> 00:39:45,355
不，我不知道。
No, I don't.

586
00:39:45,355 --> 00:39:47,315
回头见，伙计。
See you, mate.

587
00:39:54,335 --> 00:39:59,351
梅和我继续前行，熟悉的智利天气成了我们不离不弃的伙伴。
May and I drove on with the now familiar
Chilean weather our constant companion.

588
00:39:59,351 --> 00:40:03,287
我们现在在南美的曼彻斯特，
We are in the Manchester
of South America,

589
00:40:03,287 --> 00:40:05,319
但没有那烦人的口音。
but without the annoying accent.

590
00:40:05,319 --> 00:40:07,339
我要去散步。哦，不，下雨了。
I'll go for a walk.
Oh, no, it's raining.

591
00:40:07,339 --> 00:40:09,347
去打网球吧。哦，下雨了。
Let's go and play tennis.
Oh, it's raining.

592
00:40:09,347 --> 00:40:12,271
打高尔夫？哦，不，下雨了。
Round of golf?
Oh, no, it's raining.

593
00:40:12,271 --> 00:40:15,275
我要去搞园艺。哦，不，下雨了。
I'm going to do some gardening.
Oh, no, it's raining.

594
00:40:16,307 --> 00:40:19,303
随后在下一个沿海小镇，
And then in the next town,
which was on the coast,

595
00:40:19,303 --> 00:40:22,327
我发现水不一定都是从天上掉下来的。
I discovered the water doesn't
always come from the sky.

596
00:40:24,275 --> 00:40:28,307
这里的标识——海啸危险区。
This sign here -
the tsunami hazard zone.

597
00:40:28,307 --> 00:40:32,331
所以他们知道这里是易受海啸侵袭的地区，对吧。
So they know this to be an area
susceptible to tsunamis. Right.

598
00:40:35,323 --> 00:40:37,315
游乐场。
Playground.

599
00:40:38,327 --> 00:40:41,347
你干嘛那样？可以把它放那边的，那可是…
Why would you do that? You could
have put it over that side, it's...

600
00:40:41,347 --> 00:40:45,283
高出几尺，但这可是有区别的，对吧？
It's a couple of feet higher but
that makes a difference, doesn't it?

601
00:40:45,283 --> 00:40:48,315
非凡。疯狂。
这就是疯狂。
Extraordinary. Madness.
It is madness.

602
00:40:48,315 --> 00:40:51,343
我们同事终于赶到了。
Eventually our colleague arrived.

603
00:40:51,343 --> 00:40:53,363
你们俩怎么样？一切都好吧？
How are you two?
Everything all right?

604
00:40:53,363 --> 00:40:57,351
是啊，我们刚在欣赏你右边这所学校的操场位置。
Yeah, we were just enjoying
the location of this school
playground on your right.

605
00:40:57,351 --> 00:41:00,299
是啊，我对左边的消防站很感兴趣。
Yeah, I'm intrigued by the
fire station to our left.

606
00:41:00,299 --> 00:41:02,355
这……想想看，在这儿当消防员得多刺激。
That's... Imagine
being a fireman here.

607
00:41:02,355 --> 00:41:05,295
快去灭火！哦，别担心，雨已经把火扑灭了。
Quick get to the fire! Oh, don't
worry, the rain's put it out.

608
00:41:05,295 --> 00:41:08,303
也许这真的是消防站，专门来给你点火的。
Maybe it's literally a fire station,
they come and start a fire for you.

609
00:41:08,303 --> 00:41:10,319
是啊！
Yeah!

610
00:41:13,279 --> 00:41:17,275
这个镇还有 Wi‑Fi，意味着我可以下载一些
The town also had Wi-Fi,
which meant I could download some

611
00:41:17,275 --> 00:41:20,295
关于在当地道路上驾驶的官方建议。
official advice about driving
on the local roads.

612
00:41:21,295 --> 00:41:23,347
“If your vehicle has rear wheel drive...”
"If your vehicle has rear
wheel drive..."

613
00:41:23,347 --> 00:41:26,319
这很重要，和我们有关，明白吧？
Now, this is important this
applies to us, OK?

614
00:41:26,319 --> 00:41:30,335
“…recover lost control while doing speed recesses.”
"..recover lost control
while doing speed recesses."

615
00:41:30,335 --> 00:41:32,287
噢，我经历过。
Oh, I have been.

616
00:41:32,287 --> 00:41:34,311
“Avoid bite the shoulder,
"Avoid bite the shoulder,

617
00:41:34,311 --> 00:41:38,315
and if so, do not leaflet to quickly return to the asphalt.”
"and if so, do not leaflet to
quickly return to the asphalt."

618
00:41:39,351 --> 00:41:42,359
“This manoeuvre usually ends up in dumps.”
"This manoeuvre usually
ends up in dumps."

619
00:41:46,343 --> 00:41:50,367
我决定试试这种“纸上谈兵”，玩得挺开心。
I decided to try some of this
leafleting, and it was good fun.

620
00:41:50,367 --> 00:41:53,279
嗨——嗨——！
Woo-hoo-hoo!

621
00:41:53,279 --> 00:41:56,343
我的 928 后悬挂松了。
I've got a loose backend on my 928.

622
00:41:56,343 --> 00:41:59,315
虽然悬挂松，但没把车送进垃圾场。
And even though it was loose,
there were no dumps.

623
00:41:59,315 --> 00:42:01,359
呵，呵，呵！
Ho, ho, ho!

624
00:42:01,359 --> 00:42:03,339
不过在野马里……
In the Mustang, however...

625
00:42:03,339 --> 00:42:08,315
哦，不！啊！
Oh, no! Ah!

626
00:42:08,315 --> 00:42:13,367
噪音太大，哈蒙德根本听不见我们在收音机里说的任何话。
The noise was so bad, Hammond
couldn't hear a word of what
we were saying on the radio.

627
00:42:13,367 --> 00:42:17,351
哈蒙德！你牙齿刷白了，头发搞得像白痴。
Hammond! You whiten your teeth
and your hair's stupid.

628
00:42:17,351 --> 00:42:19,339
什么？
What?

629
00:42:19,339 --> 00:42:22,319
哈蒙德，听说你瘦得像教堂里的老鼠。
Hammond, I've heard you're hung
like a church mouse.

630
00:42:22,319 --> 00:42:24,307
什么？
What?

631
00:42:27,299 --> 00:42:33,275
可惜，我们的有趣游戏在看到一点一点儿不搞笑的东西后被迫中止。
Sadly, our amusing game was halted when
we spotted something that wasn't funny at all.

632
00:42:36,335 --> 00:42:41,355
又是那辆 2CV，紧跟着我们的车辙。
It is that 2CV again,
following our tracks.

633
00:42:41,355 --> 00:42:44,291
我做不到，你能做到吗？
I couldn't do that,
could you do that?

634
00:42:44,291 --> 00:42:47,367
他们怎么做到的？那帮家伙到底是谁？
How can they do that?
Who are those guys?

635
00:42:47,367 --> 00:42:51,303
别再装土匪了，拜托，别现在来这一套。
Stop doing Butch Cassidy things,
please. Not now.

636
00:42:51,303 --> 00:42:53,331
我知道是谁了。
I know who it is.

637
00:42:53,331 --> 00:42:55,291
是谁？
Who is it?

638
00:42:55,291 --> 00:43:01,283
是制作组。这就是他们所谓的搞笑备胎。
It's the producers. That's
their idea of a comedy backup car.

639
00:43:01,283 --> 00:43:05,319
我讨厌那辆 2CV，简直恨之入骨。
I hate the 2CV,
I absolutely loathe it.

640
00:43:05,319 --> 00:43:09,367
我靠在 2CV 上的试镜，直接进了原版《Top Gear》当演员，
I got a job on original Top Gear as a
result of a screen-test I did on the 2CV,

641
00:43:09,367 --> 00:43:14,323
当我光是喋喋不休、抨击那糟糕的情况足足二十分钟时，
when all I did was rant and rave for
20 minutes about how awful it was,

642
00:43:14,323 --> 00:43:16,335
而我本来还能继续怼上两个星期。
and I could have gone on
for a fortnight.

643
00:43:16,335 --> 00:43:18,311
我可不想陷进去。
I don't want to get in that.

644
00:43:18,311 --> 00:43:21,359
哈，这话倒是挺应景的，哈蒙德。闭嘴。
Well, it's funny you should
say that, Hammond. Shut up.

645
00:43:25,303 --> 00:43:29,287
我们往南开去，天气愈发糟糕
As we headed further south,
the weather got even worse

646
00:43:29,287 --> 00:43:31,307
路面简直成了噩梦。
and the road became a nightmare.

647
00:43:35,287 --> 00:43:38,275
这辆2CV真是把人叫醒了。
Very sobering, that 2CV.

648
00:43:39,319 --> 00:43:42,303
我的天啊。
Oh, my God.

649
00:43:42,303 --> 00:43:44,343
时速二十英里。
20mph.

650
00:43:46,271 --> 00:43:50,323
不出所料，我的车也在吃苦头。
Predictably, though, my car was
soaking up the punishment.

651
00:43:51,351 --> 00:43:54,279
更离谱的是，HMS Norfolk 也一样。
And amazingly, so was HMS Norfolk.

652
00:43:55,311 --> 00:43:58,287
瞧这辆莲花——已经穿过沼泽，
Look at that Lotus - it's been
through a swamp,

653
00:43:58,287 --> 00:44:01,311
又闯过森林，还依旧能跑。
it's been through a wood,
and it's still working.

654
00:44:02,319 --> 00:44:06,303
我可是把所有希望都压在这辆小红超跑上。
Quite a lot of me is rooting
for that little red super car.

655
00:44:06,303 --> 00:44:10,367
简直不可思议，我的天，谁能想到它是全球最强越野车？
It's just incredible. I mean, who knew
it was the world's best off-road car?

656
00:44:10,367 --> 00:44:15,343
谁会想到它的制造水准比雷克萨斯还高？
Who knew that it's built to a
higher standard than a Lexus?

657
00:44:15,343 --> 00:44:19,291
可是对野马来说，一切照旧。
In the Mustang, though,
it was business as usual.

658
00:44:21,311 --> 00:44:24,343
现在离合器要打滑了。
Now my clutch is starting to slip.

659
00:44:24,343 --> 00:44:26,359
又掉了一档。
I've lost another gear.

660
00:44:29,287 --> 00:44:31,295
这简直疯了，太蠢了。
This is insane, it's stupid.

661
00:44:33,359 --> 00:44:35,343
杰里米，你这条路线，
Jeremy, on this route of yours,

662
00:44:35,343 --> 00:44:38,319
到底还有多远，这玩意儿还能有多少？
how much further is it,
how much more of this?

663
00:44:39,327 --> 00:44:42,351
呃，请稍等，来电者。
Uh, stand by, caller.

664
00:44:42,351 --> 00:44:45,355
一千一百七十英里。
1,170 miles.

665
00:44:48,343 --> 00:44:50,343
一千一百？
1,100?

666
00:44:51,347 --> 00:44:53,319
再加七十，行。
And 70, yeah.

667
00:44:53,319 --> 00:44:56,343
这怎么可能，真的太离谱！
That's not possible,
for crying out loud!

668
00:45:05,335 --> 00:45:08,307
哈蒙德，我根本听不清你在说啥。
I'm not hearing a lot of what
you're saying, Hammond.

669
00:45:08,307 --> 00:45:11,287
这些车根本扛不住这折腾。
The cars absolutely
can't take the punishment.

670
00:45:11,287 --> 00:45:13,311
我的车更是撑不住。所以……
Mine certainly can't. Therefore...

671
00:45:24,335 --> 00:45:27,347
和哈蒙德不同，我可是爱上了智利。
Unlike Hammond, I was loving Chile.

672
00:45:27,347 --> 00:45:30,311
雨暂时停了一会儿，
It had stopped raining for a moment,

673
00:45:30,311 --> 00:45:33,343
风景美得让人惊叹，最棒的还有……
the scenery was wonderful,
and best of all...

674
00:45:38,287 --> 00:45:40,339
我的天！看看那玩意儿的尺寸，
Oh, my God! Look at the size
of that thing,

675
00:45:40,339 --> 00:45:42,275
真的，看看它。
seriously, look at it.

676
00:45:44,311 --> 00:45:48,295
我发誓，我从三岁起就想见到秃鹰。
I swear to God, I've wanted to see
a condor since I was about three.

677
00:45:50,339 --> 00:45:54,279
那可是全世界最大的飞禽，对吧，我觉得我说得没错？
That is the biggest flying bird in the
world, isn't it, I think I'm right in saying?

678
00:45:54,279 --> 00:45:55,347
还有另一只。
And there's another one.

679
00:46:01,331 --> 00:46:04,351
好了，太阳出来了，我看见了秃鹰，
Well, there we are - the sun's out,
I've seen a condor,

680
00:46:04,351 --> 00:46:06,343
我的世界一片光明。
all is well in my world.

681
00:46:10,287 --> 00:46:13,327
可惜，我得把这只大而漂亮的鸟儿丢下。
Sadly, I had to leave the big,
beautiful bird,

682
00:46:13,327 --> 00:46:18,303
因为到了酒店，哈蒙德已经等着对我大喊大叫了。
because at the hotel, Hammond
was waiting to shout at me.

683
00:46:18,303 --> 00:46:20,331
车内一半的装饰都掉了，真是的？
Has it?
Half the interior trim dropped off.
Has it?

684
00:46:20,331 --> 00:46:23,347
化油器全堵了，供油都不正常了。
The carburettor's all clogged up,
it doesn't fuel properly anymore.

685
00:46:23,347 --> 00:46:27,331
而且油路、变速连杆全被碎石子和砾石堵住了。
And the fuel, the gear linkage
is completely clogged up with bits
of gravel and stone

686
00:46:27,331 --> 00:46:30,283
还有泥巴和雨水，半数挡位根本用不成。
and mud and rain,
and you can't get half the gears.

687
00:46:30,283 --> 00:46:32,323
这些毛病的根源到底是什么？
And the reason for all of these
things? What?

688
00:46:32,323 --> 00:46:34,283
1970年美国制造？
Made in America in 1970?

689
00:46:34,283 --> 00:46:38,323
全是你的路线，都是你的路线，这条路简直要把车给毁了！
It's your route, it's your route,
this road is killing the car!

690
00:46:38,323 --> 00:46:42,347
哈蒙德随后掏出一张地图，嚣张地声称他找到了
Hammond then broke out a map
and boldly claimed he'd found

691
00:46:42,347 --> 00:46:46,323
一条全新的、激进的路线，通往我们的目的地。
a radical new way of getting
to our destination.

692
00:46:46,323 --> 00:46:48,339
我们要回阿根廷。为什么？
We go back to Argentina. Why?

693
00:46:48,339 --> 00:46:50,279
想想看，当我们……
Think about it, when we were...

694
00:46:50,279 --> 00:46:53,287
我们去过阿根廷，路况不错，进展顺利。
We've been to Argentina, the roads
were fine. We made good progress.

695
00:46:53,287 --> 00:46:56,275
那我们三个人都能到那里。很好，算是个成就。
Then we can all three get there.
Great, that's an achievement.

696
00:46:56,275 --> 00:46:59,323
我们至少得试试。实际上，别说试了——我们得这么干。
We've got to at least try to do it.
In fact, no - we've got to do that.

697
00:46:59,323 --> 00:47:03,311
回阿根廷……好吧……我不常这么干，但这次我要当头儿。
Back to Arg... Here's...
I don't do this very often,

698
00:47:03,311 --> 00:47:05,275
我们回阿根廷，挑条好路。
but I'm going to take charge.

699
00:47:05,275 --> 00:47:07,367
我们去过阿根廷，路况很好。
Let's go back to Argentina,
pick up the good road.

700
00:47:07,367 --> 00:47:10,295
我们会找条穿过安第斯山还能活着回来的路，
We've been to Argentina,
the roads were good.

701
00:47:10,295 --> 00:47:12,335
然后一起向南走，三个人一起。
We'll find a way across the Andes
that we can survive,

702
00:47:12,335 --> 00:47:14,347
我们还有机会以团队的姿态抵达。
and then we can head south,
all of us together.

703
00:47:14,347 --> 00:47:17,311
好啊，要是出岔子可别来找我哭鼻子。
We stand a chance
of arriving as a team.

704
00:47:17,311 --> 00:47:19,359
第二天我们一大早就起床了。
Well, don't come crying to me
if it goes wrong.

705
00:47:25,343 --> 00:47:28,275
老天，这真值了。
The next day we were up at the
crack of dawn.

706
00:47:31,307 --> 00:47:33,347
今晨真是特别。
And boy was it worth it.

707
00:47:37,347 --> 00:47:41,291
这就是老了的最大好处之一——
This is truly special this morning.

708
00:47:41,291 --> 00:47:44,311
起得早，早起的你就能看到这副景象。
This is one of the greatest
advantages of getting old -

709
00:47:44,311 --> 00:47:49,295
可是哈蒙德指挥官忙得根本没注意到智利那雾蒙蒙的道别。
you get up early, and when you
get up early, you see the world like this.

710
00:47:53,279 --> 00:47:58,323
呃……
Commander Hammond, however, was too
busy to notice Chile's misty-eyed goodbye.

711
00:47:58,323 --> 00:48:00,271
对，那是智利。
Er...

712
00:48:02,291 --> 00:48:05,271
我决定要去阿根廷更好的路面，
Right. That's Chile.

713
00:48:08,319 --> 00:48:12,303
我们应该立刻穿过安第斯山返回，
I decided that to get to the
better roads of Argentina

714
00:48:12,303 --> 00:48:15,331
这提议可没让同伴们买账。
we should head back over
the Andes immediately,

715
00:48:15,331 --> 00:48:19,359
哈蒙德，你真是，真是……
which didn't go down very well
with my colleagues.

716
00:48:19,359 --> 00:48:22,339
啊——！
Hammond, you utter, utter...

717
00:48:22,339 --> 00:48:24,355
哎呀！天啊！哈蒙德！这儿是薄冰！
Aargh!

718
00:48:24,355 --> 00:48:29,315
要是你还有一丝丝的技巧，根本不会像个白痴一样在这儿打滑。
Whoa! Christ! Hammond!
It's sheet ice here.

719
00:48:29,315 --> 00:48:34,339
我可能有点故意这么搞的。
If you possessed even an ounce of finesse
you wouldn't be slithering about like an idiot.

720
00:48:34,339 --> 00:48:36,347
我可能稍微有点故意这么做。
I might be doing it
slightly on purpose.

721
00:48:36,347 --> 00:48:39,287
商务车啊？哈哈！
Business car, eh? Ha ha!

722
00:48:39,287 --> 00:48:43,347
“哦，这就是一辆疯狂的车，它要疯了。对，真的很蠢。”
"Oh, it's just a crazy car, it goes
mental. Yeah, it's just really silly.

723
00:48:43,347 --> 00:48:47,311
“在雪地上滑来滑去。哦，看我，多有个性呀。”
"Sliding about on the snow.
Oh, look at me, full of character."

724
00:48:49,275 --> 00:48:51,367
哈蒙德向我们保证，只要我们翻过山去
Hammond assured us that once
we were over the mountains

725
00:48:51,367 --> 00:48:55,295
回到阿根廷，一切就会好起来。
and back in Argentina,
all would be well.

726
00:48:55,295 --> 00:48:56,331
但他错了。
But he was wrong.

727
00:49:01,271 --> 00:49:02,287
哎呀，天呐。
Oh, God.

728
00:49:03,307 --> 00:49:07,315
哦，对，哈蒙德，阿根廷的路可好太多了！
Oh, yeah, Hammond the roads
in Argentina are much better!

729
00:49:07,315 --> 00:49:09,367
真是他妈的。
Bloody hell.

730
00:49:09,367 --> 00:49:13,315
说实话，这根本不可接受。
This, frankly, is unacceptable.

731
00:49:14,323 --> 00:49:17,363
很快情况变得更离谱。
Soon it became even less acceptable.

732
00:49:20,299 --> 00:49:22,351
哈蒙德，我跟你要来个简短的口头交锋。
Hammond, I need a brief
exchange of words with you.

733
00:49:22,351 --> 00:49:26,291
就俩字，七个字母，三个是F。
There're only two of them, only
seven letters. Three of them are Fs.

734
00:49:27,363 --> 00:49:29,295
哎呦。
Oh, dear.

735
00:49:29,295 --> 00:49:34,319
詹姆斯，要是你说，“杰里米，你的车一点也不无聊，”
James, if you say,
"Jeremy, your car is not boring,"

736
00:49:34,319 --> 00:49:37,283
我就把你拖过去。
I will give you a tow.

737
00:49:37,283 --> 00:49:40,339
杰里米，你的车一点也不无聊，能不能把我拖一下？
Jeremy, your car isn't boring,
please would you give me a tow?

738
00:49:40,339 --> 00:49:44,283
这位高贵的德国人把勇敢的英国佬从坑里拽了出来。
The noble German helped the plucky
Brit out of the trenches.

739
00:49:45,315 --> 00:49:49,303
非常感谢，杰里米·克拉克森，还有你那辆有趣的保时捷。
Thank you very much, Jeremy
Clarkson, and your interesting Porsche.

740
00:49:50,335 --> 00:49:53,351
于是我们继续沿着哈蒙德高速公路前进，
And then we continued down
Hammond Highway,

741
00:49:53,351 --> 00:49:55,307
简直让人倒胃口。
which was appalling.

742
00:50:00,311 --> 00:50:04,331
那是什么？洗衣板——一连串近在咫尺的波纹
That? That's washboard - a whole
series of ridges very close together

743
00:50:04,331 --> 00:50:05,367
而且似乎没完没了。
and going on forever.

744
00:50:08,291 --> 00:50:10,367
哎呀！我失去二挡了。
Oh, no! I've lost second gear.

745
00:50:12,319 --> 00:50:14,327
还能再糟吗？
Still - could be worse.

746
00:50:16,339 --> 00:50:17,347
怎么了？
What's up?

747
00:50:17,347 --> 00:50:21,303
开着开着，雨刷突然启动，雨刷们，发动机也罢工了。
Driving along, the washers have
suddenly gone on, wipers,

748
00:50:21,303 --> 00:50:23,299
我可没叫它们这么干。
and the engine has stopped.

749
00:50:23,299 --> 00:50:25,311
我从没见过这种情况。
I didn't ask them to do that.

750
00:50:27,303 --> 00:50:29,363
哦，发动机又回来了。真是怪事。
I've never, ever seen
anything like that.

751
00:50:29,363 --> 00:50:33,367
好吧，来吧，继续上路。
Oh, the engine's now back.
That's really weird.

752
00:50:35,303 --> 00:50:37,339
迟早它会缺油的。
Well, come on,
let's just keep going.

753
00:50:37,339 --> 00:50:39,363
这就是哈蒙德自封为总指挥的下场。
It'll run out of fluid eventually.

754
00:50:42,363 --> 00:50:47,279
太惊人了，简直像被附身似的。
This is what happens when
Hammond puts himself in charge.

755
00:50:47,279 --> 00:50:50,275
杰里米·克拉克森和他那辆闹鬼的保时捷。
It was amazing, it
was like it was possessed.

756
00:50:50,275 --> 00:50:52,315
不对，仪表盘像圣诞树，车子已经停住了。
Jeremy Clarkson
and his haunted Porsche.

757
00:50:53,351 --> 00:50:57,347
助力转向……是死了，保时捷也挂了。
No, the dashboard is a Christmas
tree and the car has stopped.

758
00:50:57,347 --> 00:51:00,359
哔——
Power steer...
Yeah, it's dead. Porche's dead.

759
00:51:00,359 --> 00:51:03,355
哈蒙德！
BLEEP

760
00:51:03,355 --> 00:51:05,327
Hammond!
Hammond!

761
00:51:05,327 --> 00:51:07,355
这条路你选的，这下把我的保时捷给毁了。
This road you chose
has killed my Porsche.

762
00:51:07,355 --> 00:51:10,315
我可是要用棒子把你打死的。
I'm going to beat you to death
with a bat.

763
00:51:10,315 --> 00:51:12,319
为什么？什么？要是我们当时留在智利的话……
Why? What?
If we'd have stayed in Chile...

764
00:51:12,319 --> 00:51:16,315
别质疑我的领导能力，紧急情况可不是让你这么干的。
Stop questioning my leadership. That is not
what is required in an emergency situation.

765
00:51:16,315 --> 00:51:18,299
我正开着……
I'm driving along...

766
00:51:18,299 --> 00:51:20,347
这责任我自己扛。
I will deal with the responsibility.

767
00:51:20,347 --> 00:51:23,295
‘我马上就把事儿弄了。’
'And I dealt with it straight away.'

768
00:51:23,295 --> 00:51:24,331
呃……
Uh...

769
00:51:24,331 --> 00:51:25,363
‘把它抛开。’
'By leaving.'

770
00:51:27,271 --> 00:51:28,359
行，那就跟我来。
Right, then. Follow me.

771
00:51:31,367 --> 00:51:35,359
作为老大，我别无选择，信不信由你，这责任可是……
As leader, I had no choice, and believe
me, it's a responsibility that...

772
00:51:35,359 --> 00:51:39,327
我得把人留在现场，这事儿让我挺不舒服的。
It unsettles that I've
got to leave a man in the field.

773
00:51:39,327 --> 00:51:43,291
说实话，这倒挺让人担心的，因为那辆保时捷928……
Now, that is a bit of a worry, to
be honest, because the Porsche 928

774
00:51:43,291 --> 00:51:46,323
它电路一向超复杂，
was notorious for having very
complicated electrics

775
00:51:46,323 --> 00:51:48,367
而且还常出电气小妖怪，
and for having a lot
of electrical gremlins

776
00:51:48,367 --> 00:51:50,355
等它年纪大了以后。
once it got beyond a certain age.

777
00:51:51,359 --> 00:51:56,311
是啊，杰里米修好那车的可能？呃……
Yeah, Jeremy's chances of
fixing that car? Um...

778
00:51:56,311 --> 00:51:59,279
他前阵子给自己的喇叭配过线，
He did once wire his own speakers,

779
00:51:59,279 --> 00:52:02,319
也就是把插头直接塞进立体声后面，
in the sense that he plugged them
in at the back of stereo,

780
00:52:02,319 --> 00:52:06,319
在家里，你懂的，那种左右声道的小插头。
at home, you know, when you get
the little plugs, left and right.

781
00:52:09,275 --> 00:52:12,275
神奇的是，根本没我动手，
Mysteriously, without me
doing anything at all

782
00:52:12,275 --> 00:52:15,291
那保时捷居然复活了，
the Porsche had come back to life,

783
00:52:15,291 --> 00:52:17,283
大概吧。
sort of.

784
00:52:17,283 --> 00:52:21,299
好吧，雨刷停不下来，仪表盘不灵，
OK, the wipers won't turn off,
the dials aren't working,

785
00:52:21,299 --> 00:52:24,311
暖气不热，灯也不亮——
the heater isn't working,
the lights aren't working -

786
00:52:24,311 --> 00:52:27,311
但那强劲的V8又重新嗡嗡作响了！
but the mighty V8
is back in business!

787
00:52:29,315 --> 00:52:31,359
可是，走了不到一英里……
However, a mile later...

788
00:52:42,283 --> 00:52:45,307
现在发动机……哦，天呐，怎么了？
Now the engine's... Oh, Christ.
What's happened?

789
00:52:46,359 --> 00:52:49,311
那是什么玩意儿？
What is that?

790
00:52:49,311 --> 00:52:52,347
我手里有钥匙！它甩不动！
I have the key! It's off!

791
00:52:54,287 --> 00:52:57,351
发动机和启动马达一起卡死了，
The engine and the starter motor
were both jammed on,

792
00:52:57,351 --> 00:53:01,307
只能拔掉电瓶才关掉。
and they could only be shut down
by disconnecting the battery.

793
00:53:03,331 --> 00:53:07,303
这情况比我想的糟多了。
The situation is a lot worse
than I thought.

794
00:53:07,303 --> 00:53:10,339
这才是减震器顶部该有的模样。
This is what the top of the
shock absorber should look like.

795
00:53:10,339 --> 00:53:13,291
再往这边看，你会发现它被砸得——
And if you look on this side you can
see it's been punched

796
00:53:13,291 --> 00:53:17,299
脱离支架，撞上了线束，
out of its mountings and has hit
the wiring loom,

797
00:53:17,299 --> 00:53:21,335
这就是整套电路失控的原因。
which is what has made the entire
electrical system go haywire.

798
00:53:21,335 --> 00:53:24,311
现在，我还能把线束整回来，或许还能修好减震器，
Now, I can fix the wiring loom,
probably fix the shock absorber,

799
00:53:24,311 --> 00:53:27,347
但所有电器部件到底被毁成啥样了？
but what damage has been caused to
all the electrical components?

800
00:53:27,347 --> 00:53:29,279
我的意思是，灯还能亮吗？
I mean, do the lights work?

801
00:53:33,311 --> 00:53:37,343
现在已经两点半了。白天还有五个小时。
It's half past two now.
Five hours of daylight.

802
00:53:40,347 --> 00:53:47,279
与此同时，路上更远的地方，梅正收到关于当晚住宿的坏消息。
Meanwhile, further up the road,
May was getting some bad news
about that night's accommodation.

803
00:53:49,279 --> 00:53:51,323
等下，你不是在说那是个他妈的露营地吧。
Hang on, you're not saying
it's a bloody campsite.

804
00:53:51,323 --> 00:53:54,291
你把我带到了一条烂路，比我们刚才的那条还糟。
You've brought me on a crap road,
worse than the one we were on.

805
00:53:54,291 --> 00:53:56,291
我们把车子拖在路边，你把莲花车毁了
We've got a car down,
you've ruined the Lotus

806
00:53:56,291 --> 00:53:59,287
而且最后还想让我住在帐篷里！
and at the end of this you want me
to stay in a tent!

807
00:53:59,287 --> 00:54:01,327
你可能会发现帐篷杆少了一根，
You might find one of your
tent poles is missing,

808
00:54:01,327 --> 00:54:03,319
别担心，我知道它在哪儿。
but don't worry, I know where it is.

809
00:54:03,319 --> 00:54:05,279
我会把它塞进你那...
I'll have shoved it up your a...

810
00:54:05,279 --> 00:54:07,335
现在这边信号有点不稳，詹姆斯，
Signal's a bit dodgy this end
at the moment, James,

811
00:54:07,335 --> 00:54:10,283
不过我猜你那边收到信息了。
but I guess you got
the message back there.

812
00:54:12,339 --> 00:54:16,315
这就是哈蒙德的路弄得我的线束里面的情况，
This is what Hammond's road has done
to the inside of my wiring loom,

813
00:54:16,315 --> 00:54:18,335
看看这个，瞧瞧那。
look at this, just look at that.

814
00:54:18,335 --> 00:54:21,295
简直像是史蒂夫·奥斯汀的手臂内部。
It just looks like the inside of
Steve Austin's arm.

815
00:54:23,339 --> 00:54:25,363
他们还叫我猩猩，
And they call me an orang-utan,

816
00:54:25,363 --> 00:54:28,359
其实根本不知道他们在说啥。
they simply don't know what
they're talking about.

817
00:54:31,275 --> 00:54:33,295
在一段悲惨的驾驶之后
At the end of a miserable drive

818
00:54:33,295 --> 00:54:36,275
我现在不得不面对晚上的露营。
I was now faced with
an evening's tenting.

819
00:54:37,287 --> 00:54:40,299
整整一天在糟糕的路上开车，把我的车弄得一团糟，
A whole day driving on a
terrible road, wrecking my car,

820
00:54:40,299 --> 00:54:44,303
可能还会把保时捷弄丢，弄断了脊椎，
possibly losing the Porsche,
breaking my spine,

821
00:54:44,303 --> 00:54:47,359
随后哈蒙德说我得搭起帐篷，他自己去弄吃的。
then Hammond says I have to put the
tent up while he goes off to get the food.

822
00:54:47,359 --> 00:54:50,323
我根本不知道他的帐篷怎么装的，而他却清楚
And I don't know how his tent
goes together, and he knows

823
00:54:50,323 --> 00:54:55,283
对食物和烹饪的事了如指掌，哔——
absolutely the square root of jack
BLEEP about food and cooking.

824
00:54:55,283 --> 00:54:58,367
我想知道还有没有人... 我想知道观众们会不会觉得哈蒙德的
I wonder if anybody else... I
wonder if the viewers find Hammond's

825
00:54:58,367 --> 00:55:04,327
那种轻快、阳光、像罗斯·温（Ross-on-Wye）的口吻会不会跟我一样让人恼火？
chirpy, upbeat, Ross-on-Wye
mannerisms as aggravating as I do?

826
00:55:06,311 --> 00:55:10,339
好了，现在都贴好胶带了，看看能不能启动。
Right, everything is now taped up,
so let's see if it starts.

827
00:55:19,347 --> 00:55:20,367
好了，给你。
There you go.

828
00:55:22,331 --> 00:55:26,347
在营地，我端着我们的晚餐回来。
At the campsite, I was returning
with our evening meal.

829
00:55:28,283 --> 00:55:29,331
希望他饿了。
I hope he's hungry.

830
00:55:33,287 --> 00:55:35,347
喂！喂！
Hello! Hello!

831
00:55:35,347 --> 00:55:37,355
晚餐到了。
Dinner is here.

832
00:55:37,355 --> 00:55:39,327
是啊！
Yeah!

833
00:55:39,327 --> 00:55:41,295
肉啊。是啊，真是太好笑了，量不少。
Meat. Yeah, very funny A lot of it.

834
00:55:41,295 --> 00:55:44,359
是啊，不过我们已经开过这个玩笑了，因为杰里米在美国北部也这么说过。是啊。
Yeah, but we've done that joke, cos Jeremy
did it in the top part of America. Yeah.

835
00:55:44,359 --> 00:55:47,335
大概七、八年前的事，你可能已经忘了。
About seven or eight years ago,
you've probably forgotten.

836
00:55:47,335 --> 00:55:50,271
这次不一样，这次更好。
This time it's different,
this time it's better.

837
00:55:50,271 --> 00:55:52,351
你要面对的... 不，听着。
What you're going to have...
No, listen.

838
00:55:52,351 --> 00:55:55,367
是一场传统、正宗的高乔烤肉。
..is a traditional, authentic
gaucho barbecue.

839
00:55:55,367 --> 00:55:57,307
那可是整头牛啊。
That's a whole cow.

840
00:55:57,307 --> 00:55:59,315
嘿，这儿的人肉吃得可真多。
Hey, they eat a lot of meat
round here.

841
00:55:59,315 --> 00:56:04,291
把帐篷装好，我马上装上。说真的，快干吧。
Finish the tent. I'll have it on
in a moment. Seriously. Crack on.

842
00:56:04,291 --> 00:56:05,303
好的。
Right.

843
00:56:07,339 --> 00:56:10,355
根本问题就是把外包装剥下来。
It's a problem, essentially,
of getting the wrapper off.

844
00:56:14,335 --> 00:56:19,339
经过几小时的剥皮后，哈蒙德的晚饭已经开动。
Several hours of peeling later,
Hammond's dinner was underway.

845
00:56:19,339 --> 00:56:24,275
我们吃着饭，聊起了那位同事的下场。
And while we ate, we discussed
the fate of our colleague.

846
00:56:24,275 --> 00:56:29,327
如果我们听到两声…呃，也可能是一根气缸的声音，
If we hear the sound of two...
Well, or one cylinder,

847
00:56:29,327 --> 00:56:32,343
那大概就是2CV了。是啊。
it's probably the 2CV. Yeah.

848
00:56:32,343 --> 00:56:36,307
但要是超过两声，那肯定是保时捷的。
But any more than two,
it must be the Porsche.

849
00:56:36,307 --> 00:56:39,311
要是他因为蠢得修不出来，结果…？
What if he couldn't fix it
because he's stupid and ended up...?

850
00:56:39,311 --> 00:56:41,319
不，他可是电路专家。
No, but he's an expert on electrics.

851
00:56:41,319 --> 00:56:43,299
等等，那是发动机啊。
Hang on that's an engine.

852
00:56:46,339 --> 00:56:49,287
到底是啥？
What is it?

853
00:56:49,287 --> 00:56:51,335
就是全世界最不开心的人，真的。
It's the unhappiest man
in the world, is what it is.

854
00:56:51,335 --> 00:56:53,335
哎呀，糟了！
Oh, no!

855
00:56:53,335 --> 00:56:57,367
哎呀，真的……我真以为会是……
Oh, no! I really...
I honestly thought that would be...

856
00:57:00,275 --> 00:57:03,315
等下，那…它在跟踪我们。看啊！
Oh, hang on. That...
It's stalking us. There it is!

857
00:57:04,363 --> 00:57:08,275
他一定得意洋洋。
He's going to be
so pleased with himself.

858
00:57:08,275 --> 00:57:11,303
我一直在干体力活。
I have been doing manual labour.

859
00:57:11,303 --> 00:57:13,279
天呐，真的？
Good God. Really?

860
00:57:13,279 --> 00:57:16,291
我不太愿意承认，但我真的在祈祷保时捷出现。
I hardly like to admit it, but I was praying
that the Porsche would turn up.

861
00:57:16,291 --> 00:57:18,339
我不想看它挂掉。那简直太棒了。
I didn't want to see it die.
That is absolutely fabulous.

862
00:57:18,339 --> 00:57:22,319
我真的弄脏了手，真正的活儿弄得手脏。到底是干啥的？
I've actually got dirty hands from
actual work. Dirty hands. What was it?

863
00:57:22,319 --> 00:57:25,307
我得修理线轴，调试ECU，
I had to fix the loom, fix the ECU,

864
00:57:25,307 --> 00:57:29,283
然后找点金属，把它螺栓固定在内翼上
and then find some metal,
bolt that to the inner wing

865
00:57:29,283 --> 00:57:32,355
再把减震器的顶部重新装上。
and reattach the top of
the shock absorber to that.

866
00:57:32,355 --> 00:57:35,299
哦，干得好。有给我准备的吃的吗？
Oh, well done.
Have you got any food for me?

867
00:57:35,299 --> 00:57:37,315
哦，他有吗？！啊！
Oh, has he?! Ah!

868
00:57:37,315 --> 00:57:40,355
我记不全……想不起来它从哪来的，
I'm not entire... I can't
remember where it came from,

869
00:57:40,355 --> 00:57:42,291
我有点糊涂了。
I sort of lost track.

870
00:57:42,291 --> 00:57:45,367
牛里东西很多。那是…嗯，那是一块。
There's a lot in a cow.
That's... Um, that's a piece of it.

871
00:57:45,367 --> 00:57:48,339
我们有蔬菜吗？
Have we got any vegetables?

872
00:57:48,339 --> 00:57:51,303
那边那是蔬菜吗？对，对，香肠。
Is that a vegetable over here?
Yeah. Yeah, sausages.

873
00:57:51,303 --> 00:57:53,335
欢迎来到我们的营地，这才是重点。
Welcome to our little camp,
that's the main thing.

874
00:57:53,335 --> 00:57:56,327
好吧，我们住的旅馆在哪？
Right, where is the hotel
where we're staying?

875
00:57:56,327 --> 00:57:59,343
我刚说——欢迎来到我们的营地。
Well, I just said -
welcome to our little camp.

876
00:57:59,343 --> 00:58:01,271
啥？
What?

877
00:58:04,303 --> 00:58:07,347
那天晚上，杰里米睡得很郁闷。
Jeremy went to sleep that night
quite cross.

878
00:58:07,347 --> 00:58:12,275
于是，为了让他高兴，梅和我想了个办法。
So, to cheer him up, May and I
came up with a plan.

879
00:58:12,275 --> 00:58:15,275
就那个。好，我来搞这些。
That one.
Right, I'll do these bits.

880
00:58:15,275 --> 00:58:18,271
问题是，最终这对他根本没用。
The thing is, it's not making any
difference to him, ultimately.

881
00:58:18,271 --> 00:58:21,275
这居然对我们的生活有点影响。
It's making a difference to our
lives.

882
00:58:21,275 --> 00:58:23,323
哦！还挺不错的。
Oh! That's quite good.

883
00:58:23,323 --> 00:58:24,363
“挺不错”？！
"Quite good"?!

884
00:58:24,363 --> 00:58:27,291
我把它关掉。 好了，还有什么别的？
I'm turning that off.
Right, what else have we got?

885
00:58:27,291 --> 00:58:29,311
另一边还有一个那玩意儿。
Another one of those
on the other side.

886
00:58:34,343 --> 00:58:37,283
他们胯骨的每根骨头。
Every bone in their crotches.

887
00:58:38,319 --> 00:58:40,299
这就是我要砸的。
That's what I'm going to break.

888
00:58:47,307 --> 00:58:49,315
你干嘛干这玩意儿？
Why have you done this?

889
00:58:49,315 --> 00:58:52,335
没事儿，你可以看看一辆 Esprit 和一辆 Mustang，
It's all right, you get to look at
an Esprit and a Mustang,

890
00:58:52,335 --> 00:58:55,275
我们得整天盯着这玩意儿，超无聊。
we have to look at this all day,
and it's dull.

891
00:58:55,275 --> 00:58:57,271
我们把它弄亮了。
We've brightened it up.

892
00:58:57,271 --> 00:59:00,283
你有西装吗？有的。是定制的还是买的？
Have you got a suit? Yes, I have.
Did you have it made, did you buy it?

893
00:59:00,283 --> 00:59:04,283
你是说，‘能给它装点金色肩章再贴个 Happy Mondays 徽章吗’？
Did you say, "Could you put some gold
epaulets on it and a Happy Mondays badge?

894
00:59:04,283 --> 00:59:06,347
‘能给我加个彩虹骄傲的内衬吗？’ 你这么说了？没有。
"Can I have a Gay Pride lining?"
Did you say that? No.

895
00:59:06,347 --> 00:59:10,291
是啊，但我才不让你每天盯着我这套无聊的西装。
Yeah, but I wouldn't make you look at
me in my boring suit day after day.

896
00:59:10,291 --> 00:59:12,351
我们被迫天天看着你那辆无聊的车。
We're obliged to look at you
in your boring car.

897
00:59:12,351 --> 00:59:15,355
现在我们来看看这玩意儿，有点意思的造型点散落其间。
Now we look at something with some
interesting styling cues dashed about.

898
00:59:15,355 --> 00:59:18,323
不，它看起来像个五岁小孩穿妈妈的鞋子。
No, it looks like a five-year-old
wearing its mother's shoes.

899
00:59:18,323 --> 00:59:21,279
好吧，这比之前有点意思了，稍微好点。
Well, that's more interesting
than it was. It's better.

900
00:59:21,279 --> 00:59:23,287
干嘛不把篝火灭了，
Why don't you put the campfire out,

901
00:59:23,287 --> 00:59:24,307
直接用你的脸当灯？
and use your face.

902
00:59:25,315 --> 00:59:27,315
还有件事儿。
And there's one more thing, as well.

903
00:59:29,331 --> 00:59:31,367
那是我的地图。
That's my map.

904
00:59:31,367 --> 00:59:34,327
你免去指挥权了。 我同意。
You're relieved of command.
I'm with that.

905
00:59:39,307 --> 00:59:41,367
一出发，天气立刻变脸儿。
As we set off,
the weather closed in.

906
00:59:43,335 --> 00:59:44,363
我可不爽这个。
I don't like this.

907
00:59:46,351 --> 00:59:51,279
大雪里，我又发现同事们的喜剧段子。
And in the blizzard, I discovered
another comedy jape from my colleagues.

908
00:59:52,303 --> 00:59:53,355
我的天哪……？
What in God's name...?

909
00:59:54,367 --> 00:59:59,319
你怎么在仪表盘上装了个刹车灯？
Why have you fitted my car with
a brake light on the dash board.

910
00:59:59,319 --> 01:00:02,327
好啊，监视你自己的刹车倒是挺有意思的。
Well, it'll be interesting to
monitor your own braking.

911
01:00:02,327 --> 01:00:03,339
是吗？真的吗？
Is it? Is it?

912
01:00:05,359 --> 01:00:08,355
詹姆斯和理查德这类人，居然会把
James and Richard are the sort
of people that would put

913
01:00:08,355 --> 01:00:10,343
乌龟倒着背过去玩儿。
a tortoise on its back, for fun.

914
01:00:14,367 --> 01:00:19,279
说实话，我确实遇到了一些真问题。
In truth, though, I did have some
genuine problems.

915
01:00:19,279 --> 01:00:23,331
我的时速表、转速表、油压表、油量表，
My speedo, my rev counter,
oil pressure gauge, fuel gauge,

916
01:00:23,331 --> 01:00:27,315
温度表、行程电脑，全都罢工了。
temperature gauge,
my trip computer, all dead.

917
01:00:29,279 --> 01:00:32,279
哈蒙德的车也好不到哪儿去。
Hammond's car wasn't much better.

918
01:00:32,279 --> 01:00:34,331
呃，还有谁闻到烧焦味了吗？
Um, can anyone else smell burning?

919
01:00:36,291 --> 01:00:40,291
而我们还得再开 900 英里。
And we still had 900 miles to go.

920
01:00:44,275 --> 01:00:45,359
那是个干枯的湖床。
It was a dried up lake bed.

921
01:00:45,359 --> 01:00:48,295
我现在把它当成赛道了
I see it now as a racetrack

922
01:00:48,295 --> 01:00:50,343
哦，那是……！啊呀！
Oh, that was...!
Argh!

923
01:00:50,343 --> 01:00:52,351
你还能记得路在哪儿吗？
Can you remember where the road was?

924
01:00:54,275 --> 01:00:55,327
这真是个错误。
This was a mistake.

925
01:00:55,327 --> 01:00:56,331
赶紧上车吧。
Just get on.

926
01:00:59,359 --> 01:01:03,271
这玩意儿太他妈危险了，真是危险。
It's bloody dangerous, this.
Bloody dangerous.

927
01:01:06,367 --> 01:01:10,347
我在诺福克宣称这片地，叫它莲花海滩。
I claim this land for Norfolk
and name it Lotus Beach.

928
01:01:13,307 --> 01:01:15,275
拜托让开，保时捷，让开。
Please move, Porsche, please move.

929
01:01:17,311 --> 01:01:20,355
来啦！这是拉力赛道。
There you go! Rally stage.

930
01:01:20,355 --> 01:01:24,295
我没跟他说我背疼。哎呀！
I didn't tell him I had a bad back.
Aya!

931
01:01:24,295 --> 01:01:28,323
抵达乌斯怀亚，建个体育场，踢足球，搞外交。
Arrive Ushuaia, build stadium,
play football, do diplomacy.

932
01:01:28,323 --> 01:01:30,347
还能出啥岔子？
What can possibly go wrong
with that?

933
01:01:30,347 --> 01:01:35,271
自行车跟在明星车后面，自行车跟在明星车后面。
Bikes behind the star cars,
bikes behind the star cars.

934
01:01:35,271 --> 01:01:36,563
他们在找那辆保时捷。
They're looking for the Porsche.

935
